# Runbook: GitHub Copilot AI Asset Inventory Record (OneTrust)

## Purpose
Establish and maintain a formal AI/ML asset record for **GitHub Copilot — Engineering Code Review** in the OneTrust AI Governance module, ensuring ownership, data classification, risk tier, and escalation triggers are documented and recertified on a 90-day cycle.

---

## Prerequisites
- OneTrust AI Governance module licensed and accessible
- OneTrust Administrator or AI Governance Manager role
- Agreement from Engineering VP (Business Owner) and DevOps Lead (Technical Owner) to accept named ownership

---

## Step 1 — Create the AI/ML Asset Record

1. Log in to **OneTrust** → navigate to **AI Governance** → **Inventory**.
2. Click **+ Add Asset** → select type **AI/ML Tool (Third-Party)**.
3. Set the following fields:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Asset Name | `GitHub Copilot — Engineering Code Review` |
| Vendor | `GitHub / Microsoft` |
| Asset Status | `Active` |
| Deployment Scope | `All GitHub Organization repositories` |
| Access Scope | `All private repos including IaC (infra-*, terraform-*, security-*)` |

---

## Step 2 — Populate Ownership

| Role | Person / Title | TODO |
|---|---|---|
| Business Owner | Engineering VP | `# TODO: replace with named individual and email` |
| Technical Owner | DevOps Lead | `# TODO: replace with named individual and email` |
| Privacy Contact | Legal / Privacy Counsel | `# TODO: replace with named individual` |
| Security Contact | InfoSec Lead | `# TODO: replace with named individual` |

---

## Step 3 — Data Classification

Record the following **Data Categories** processed by Copilot:

- Proprietary source code (all languages)
- IaC configurations (Terraform `.tf`, `.tfvars`, HCL)
- Internal libraries and shared modules
- Security configurations (firewall rules, network topology definitions)
- Classification level: **Confidential / Proprietary**

> `# TODO: Verify classification levels against your organization''s data classification policy.`

---

## Step 4 — Risk Tier

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Accepted Risk Tier | `High` (processes confidential IP; vendor-managed model) |
| Risk Acceptance Owner | Engineering VP |
| Risk Acceptance Date | `# TODO: insert date` |
| Next Review Date | 90 days from acceptance date |

---

## Step 5 — Escalation Triggers (T1–T6)

Link the following conditions as **Review Conditions** in the OneTrust record. Any trigger should initiate an immediate out-of-cycle review.

| Trigger ID | Condition |
|---|---|
| T1 | GitHub/Microsoft announces a change to Copilot data handling or training opt-out policy |
| T2 | A new secret scanning alert is confirmed in any Copilot-scoped repository |
| T3 | Copilot license scope is expanded beyond the `Copilot-Licensed-Engineers` group |
| T4 | A new IaC or security-sensitive repository is added to the GitHub Organization |
| T5 | A data breach or security incident is reported by GitHub/Microsoft affecting Copilot |
| T6 | Organization undergoes M&A, divestiture, or material change in engineering headcount (>20%) |

> `# TODO: Validate trigger definitions with Legal, InfoSec, and Engineering VP before recording.`

---

## Step 6 — Recertification Cycle

1. In OneTrust, set **Recertification Frequency** to **90 days**.
2. Assign recertification task to: Business Owner (Engineering VP) and Technical Owner (DevOps Lead).
3. Recertification checklist (each cycle):
   - [ ] Confirm access scope (repos, user group) is unchanged or document changes
   - [ ] Confirm opt-out settings still active (cross-reference Pillar 3 controls)
   - [ ] Review T1–T6 triggers — any triggered since last cycle?
   - [ ] Confirm DPA is current and sub-processor list unchanged
   - [ ] Update risk tier if warranted
   - [ ] Sign off and record date in OneTrust

---

## Step 7 — Jira Integration (Recurring Task)

Create a Jira recurring task in the Security/Compliance project:

```
Project:   # TODO: replace with your Jira project key (e.g., SEC)
Summary:   [Quarterly] Recertify GitHub Copilot OneTrust Inventory Record
Assignee:  DevOps Lead
Reviewer:  Engineering VP
Recurs:    Every 90 days from initial creation date
Labels:    ai-governance, copilot, recertification
Description:
  Review and re-sign the GitHub Copilot AI asset record in OneTrust.
  Checklist items are documented in the runbook:
  onetrust_copilot_inventory_record.md
```

---

