# GitHub Copilot — Ownership & Governance Runbook

**Version:** 1.0 <!-- TODO: increment on each review -->
**Business Owner:** <!-- TODO: Engineering VP / Director name and email -->
**Technical Owner:** <!-- TODO: DevOps / Platform Engineering Lead name and email -->
**OneTrust Asset:** GitHub Copilot <!-- TODO: confirm exact asset name and ID in OneTrust -->
**Jira Recurring Task:** <!-- TODO: insert Jira ticket ID for quarterly re-attestation -->
**Review Cadence:** Quarterly

---

## 1. Purpose

This runbook defines the ownership model and quarterly re-attestation process for the GitHub Copilot deployment. Named owners are accountable for configuration governance, escalation trigger monitoring, and periodic risk review.

---

## 2. Owner Responsibilities

### Business Owner (Engineering VP / Director)

| Responsibility | Frequency |
|---|---|
| Approve any change to Copilot org-level policies (e.g., seat expansion, new feature enablement) | As-needed |
| Sign off on quarterly re-attestation | Quarterly |
| Escalation point for `AI-Concern` Jira tickets that are HIGH/CRITICAL | Within 2 business days |
| Ensure Copilot is represented in OneTrust AI risk inventory | Ongoing |

### Technical Owner (DevOps / Platform Lead)

| Responsibility | Frequency |
|---|---|
| Monitor GitHub Org Settings for auto-enabled new Copilot features | Weekly <!-- TODO: consider automating via GitHub audit log export to Datadog --> |
| Triage incoming `AI-Concern` Jira tickets | Within 2 business days |
| Maintain branch protection and CI scan configurations | Ongoing |
| Lead quarterly re-attestation checklist | Quarterly |
| Maintain user acknowledgment tracking in Jira | Ongoing |

---

## 3. OneTrust AI Inventory Registration

1. Log into OneTrust. <!-- TODO: confirm OneTrust instance URL -->
2. Navigate to **Inventory → AI Systems**.
3. Open or create the record for **GitHub Copilot**.
4. Populate the following fields:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Business Owner | <!-- TODO: Engineering VP name + email --> |
| Technical Owner | <!-- TODO: Platform Lead name + email --> |
| Risk Classification | <!-- TODO: e.g., Medium — AI-assisted code generation --> |
| Data Processed | Source code (proprietary), IaC configs |
| Training Opt-Out Status | Confirmed OFF (Copilot org policy) <!-- TODO: verify and document --> |
| Public Code Block | Confirmed ON (see control cd71b730) |
| Review Date | <!-- TODO: YYYY-MM-DD --> |
| Next Review Date | <!-- TODO: YYYY-MM-DD + 90 days --> |

5. Attach evidence: screenshot of GitHub Org > Copilot > Policies settings page.

---

## 4. Quarterly Re-Attestation Checklist

> This checklist is executed by the Technical Owner, signed off by the Business Owner, and recorded in the OneTrust asset record. A recurring Jira task (type: `Copilot-Governance-Review`) should be created and assigned to both owners every 90 days.
> <!-- TODO: Create the Jira automation rule to generate this recurring task -->

### 4.1 Configuration Verification

- [ ] Log into GitHub Org Settings > Copilot > Policies.
- [ ] Confirm **"Suggestions matching public code"** is set to **Blocked**.
- [ ] Confirm **"Allow GitHub to use my code snippets for product improvements"** (training opt-out) is **disabled/off** for the org. <!-- TODO: verify current GitHub UI label -->
- [ ] Confirm no new Copilot features have been **auto-enabled** since last review (check GitHub changelog and audit log).
- [ ] Confirm seat count matches active licensed engineers list. Remove any departed employees.

### 4.2 Branch Protection & CI Scan Verification

- [ ] Spot-check 3 Copilot-enabled repos: confirm branch protection rules are in place on `main`.
- [ ] Confirm the `iac-security-scan` required status check is active on all IaC repos.
- [ ] Review any checkov/tfsec suppression comments added in the last quarter; ensure each has documented justification.

### 4.3 Escalation Trigger Review

- [ ] Review all `AI-Concern` Jira tickets opened in the last 90 days.
- [ ] Confirm all tickets are resolved or have an active owner.
- [ ] Identify any patterns (e.g., recurring insecure IAM suggestions) that warrant a policy or prompt change.

### 4.4 User Acknowledgment Audit

- [ ] Pull list of all Copilot-licensed engineers from GitHub Org.
- [ ] Cross-reference against completed `Copilot-AUP-Acknowledgment` Jira tasks.
- [ ] Follow up with any engineers who have not acknowledged the Acceptable Use Policy.

### 4.5 Sign-Off

| Role | Name | Date | Signature / Jira task closed |
|---|---|---|---|
| Technical Owner | <!-- TODO --> | | |
| Business Owner | <!-- TODO --> | | |

- [ ] Upload completed checklist as evidence attachment to the OneTrust GitHub Copilot asset record.
- [ ] Update **Next Review Date** in OneTrust to current date + 90 days.

---

## 5. Escalation Path

```
AI-Concern Jira ticket raised by engineer
        │
        ▼
Technical Owner triages (≤ 2 business days)
        │
        ├─ LOW/MEDIUM → Technical Owner resolves, documents in Jira
        │
        └─ HIGH/CRITICAL → Escalate to Business Owner (≤ same day)
                │
                └─ If data/IP risk → Engage Legal / CISO
                   <!-- TODO: insert Legal/CISO contact --> 
```

