# GitHub Copilot Quarterly Vendor AI Feature Review

## Purpose
Ensure that every new Copilot capability, data-handling change, or opt-out posture shift is assessed before it reaches production engineers — and that findings are recorded in OneTrust and tracked in Jira.

---

## Trigger
Recurring quarterly. A Jira Epic **"GitHub Copilot Vendor Review — Q[N] [YEAR]"** must be created at the start of each quarter and closed with documented sign-off before the quarter ends.

> **TODO:** Assign the Epic to the technical owner.
> **TODO:** Set the Jira project key (e.g., `SEC`, `AI-GOV`).
> **TODO:** Set due date = last working day of the quarter.

---

## Jira Epic Structure

Create the following child stories under the Epic each quarter:

| Story Key | Title | Owner |
|-----------|-------|-------|
| TASK-1 | Review GitHub Copilot Changelog | Technical Owner |
| TASK-2 | Audit Org Settings for Auto-Enabled Features | Technical Owner |
| TASK-3 | Re-verify Training Opt-Out & Telemetry via API | Technical Owner |
| TASK-4 | Escalation Trigger Assessment (T1–T6) | Security Lead |
| TASK-5 | Update OneTrust Vendor Record | Compliance / GRC Owner |
| TASK-6 | Epic Sign-Off & Close | Technical Owner + Security Lead |

---

## Task Procedures

### TASK-1 — Review GitHub Copilot Changelog
1. Navigate to: <https://github.blog/changelog/> — filter tag **"GitHub Copilot"**.
2. Review all entries since the last quarterly review date.
3. Flag any entries touching: agent mode, Workspace, CLI, data residency, model upgrades, new IDE integrations.
4. Log flagged items as sub-tasks under TASK-1 with a brief risk note.

### TASK-2 — Audit Org Settings for Auto-Enabled Features
1. Go to **GitHub Organization Settings → Copilot → Policies**.
   > **TODO:** Replace `YOUR-ORG` below with your GitHub organization slug.
2. Verify the following settings match the approved baseline:
   - **Suggestions matching public code**: `Blocked`
   - **Copilot in github.com**: only enabled for approved users/teams
   - **Copilot Chat in IDE**: confirm enabled/disabled per policy
   - **Copilot Workspace / Agent Mode**: confirm enabled/disabled per policy
   - **CLI extension**: confirm enabled/disabled per policy
3. Capture a screenshot or export settings via API:
   ```bash
   # TODO: Replace ORG and TOKEN values
   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_GITHUB_PAT" \
        -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
        "https://api.github.com/orgs/YOUR-ORG/copilot/billing"
   ```
4. Attach the output to the Jira story.

### TASK-3 — Re-verify Training Opt-Out & Telemetry Settings
1. Confirm **"Allow GitHub to use my data to improve Copilot"** is **OFF** at org level:
   - GitHub Org Settings → Copilot → Policies → **"Allow GitHub to use my organization''s data for product improvements"** = **Disabled**.
2. Verify via API:
   ```bash
   # TODO: Replace ORG and TOKEN values
   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_GITHUB_PAT" \
        -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
        "https://api.github.com/orgs/YOUR-ORG/copilot/billing"
   # Check: "public_code_suggestions", "seat_management_setting"
   ```
3. Document the exact API response and confirm opt-out fields.
4. If training opt-out is found **enabled**, treat as a **Tier 6 escalation trigger** — follow the Copilot Incident Response runbook immediately.

### TASK-4 — Escalation Trigger Assessment (T1–T6)
For each trigger, mark **Triggered / Not Triggered / N/A** and provide evidence:

| Trigger | Description | Status | Evidence |
|---------|-------------|--------|----------|
| T1 | New autonomous capability detected (agent mode, multi-repo) | | |
| T2 | Data handling policy change by vendor | | |
| T3 | Model upgrade with different training data scope | | |
| T4 | New telemetry or logging capability introduced | | |
| T5 | Copilot access expanded beyond approved user set | | |
| T6 | Training opt-out reversed or no longer honoured | | |

If **any trigger fires**, escalate per the Copilot Incident Response runbook.
> **TODO:** Link the incident runbook URL here.

### TASK-5 — Update OneTrust Vendor Record
1. Log into OneTrust → Vendor/Third-Party Risk module.
   > **TODO:** Insert the OneTrust vendor record URL for GitHub Copilot.
2. Update the following fields:
   - **Last Review Date**: today''s date
   - **Reviewer**: Technical Owner name
   - **Data Handling Status**: confirmed opt-out = Yes/No
   - **New Features Identified**: list from TASK-1
   - **Escalation Triggers Fired**: list from TASK-4 (or "None")
   - **Next Review Due**: first week of next quarter
3. Attach the Jira Epic link and API outputs as evidence artifacts.

### TASK-6 — Epic Sign-Off
1. Technical Owner reviews all child story completions.
2. Security Lead countersigns (Jira comment with explicit "Approved" + date).
3. Close the Epic with resolution = **"Done"**.
4. If any trigger was fired and an incident opened, do **not** close the Epic until the incident is resolved.

