#    Replace matches with "[REDACTED]" and log the hit with the source document ID.
#
# 4. LOGGING — emit a structured log entry for every sanitization hit:
#    { "event": "rag_injection_pattern_detected",
#      "document_id": "<azure_ai_search_doc_id>",
#      "pattern_matched": "<pattern>",
#      "timestamp": "<ISO8601>",
#      "session_id": "<session>" }
#    Route these logs to the Sentinel/Splunk workspace for alerting.
#    TODO: wire log sink to your Application Insights / Log Analytics workspace.
#
# 5. VALIDATION GATE — if more than N patterns are stripped from a single
#    retrieved chunk, abort the request and surface an error to the user rather
#    than proceeding with a sanitized but potentially compromised context.
#    TODO: tune N based on baseline testing (suggested starting value: 3).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

echo "==> Done. Review orchestration-layer requirements in the script comments."
