INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('6e415c47-d7f2-468d-94dd-edcd73b1fe59', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '97cd8230-e2e2-47e4-944a-e5896b5ef796', 8, 'Conduct a decision impact assessment documenting the consequences of AI false negatives (missed risky clauses) and false positives (spurious flags) across contract types, including financial exposure thresholds and regulatory consequences.', 'The top risk is false negatives that the legal team never sees; without a documented impact assessment, the organization cannot set appropriate severity thresholds, sampling rates, or decide which contract categories require heightened scrutiny.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-10T03:46:26.461699+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9 (risk management); Art. 14 (human oversight)","iso_42001":"A.5.4; A.6.2.6","owasp_llm":"LLM09 Overreliance","nist_ai_rmf":"MAP 2.1; MAP 2.2; MEASURE 3.3"}'::jsonb, 'Create a Confluence page under the AI inventory titled ''Contract Review AI — Decision Impact Assessment''. Template sections: (1) False negative impact by contract type and value tier, (2) False positive impact, (3) Acceptable error rates, (4) Mitigating controls mapped to each scenario. Assign to the rule set owner and Legal team lead for co-authorship. Link to the AI inventory Epic in Jira. Review annually or upon material system change.', 'Decision impact assessment document covering: false negative scenarios by contract type with estimated financial/legal impact, false positive cost (reviewer time waste, workflow delays), acceptable error rates by contract category, and mitigating controls for each scenario.', 'Review the impact assessment for completeness — confirm it covers at least 3 contract categories, quantifies financial exposure for false negatives, and the acceptable error rates are referenced in the test suite pass thresholds.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'runbook', 'markdown', 'contract_review_ai_decision_impact_assessment.md', '# Contract Review AI — Decision Impact Assessment
## Control: 6e415c47-d7f2-468d-94dd-edcd73b1fe59

**Purpose:** Document the consequences of AI false negatives (missed risky clauses) and false positives (spurious flags) across contract types, including financial exposure thresholds and regulatory consequences. This assessment informs severity thresholds, sampling rates, and scrutiny levels.

**Ownership:** Rule Set Owner (AI/Contract Review Program) + Legal Team Lead  
**Review Cadence:** Annually or within 30 days of material system change  
**Location:** Link in Jira Epic [TODO: INSERT_EPIC_KEY]; host in Confluence under AI Inventory  

---

## 1. False Negative Impact by Contract Type and Value Tier

### 1.1 Definition
A false negative occurs when the AI model fails to flag a risky clause (e.g., unfavorable IP assignment, unlimited liability cap, auto-renewal, indemnification overreach) that legal review *should* have caught.

### 1.2 Impact Matrix: Contract Type vs. Value Tier

| Contract Type | Low Value (<$50k) | Mid Value ($50k–$500k) | High Value (>$500k) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Software License / SaaS** | Financial: $5k–$25k remediation; Regulatory: Low | Financial: $50k–$250k exposure; Regulatory: Potential data breach notification | Financial: $500k+ escrow/termination risk; Regulatory: GDPR/CCPA consent gaps |
| **Vendor Agreement / MSA** | Financial: Operational cost overrun ~$10k; Regulatory: Low | Financial: $100k+ scope creep; Regulatory: Audit compliance gaps | Financial: $1M+ penalty clauses; Regulatory: Industry certification risk |
| **Data Processing / DPA** | Financial: $5k notification cost; Regulatory: **CRITICAL**—GDPR/CCPA Article 28 breach | Financial: $50k+ fines; Regulatory: DPA enforcement action | Financial: $250k+ statutory penalties; Regulatory: Data controller liability |
| **Service Level / SOW** | Financial: Service credit $5k–$10k; Regulatory: Low | Financial: Service credit $50k–$100k; Regulatory: Performance reporting gap | Financial: $500k+ breach cascade; Regulatory: Availability/security threshold violation |
| **IP / Confidentiality** | Financial: Trade secret exposure $10k–$50k; Regulatory: Low | Financial: $100k+ market damage; Regulatory: Potential misappropriation suit | Financial: $1M+ core IP leak; Regulatory: Antitrust/regulatory disclosure |

### 1.3 Examples of High-Impact False Negatives
- **Missed auto-renewal clause** in $2M SaaS contract → 2-year unintended commitment
- **Uncaught indemnification overreach** in vendor MSA → exposure to third-party claims without limitation
- **Overlooked data subprocessor clause** in DPA → GDPR Article 28 non-compliance; fines up to 4% revenue
- **Silent IP assignment on derivative works** in $500k development contract → loss of improvements

---

## 2. False Positive Impact

### 2.1 Definition
A false positive occurs when the AI flags a clause as risky when it is actually market-standard, benign, or already acceptable to legal.

### 2.2 Operational & Reputational Costs

| Impact Type | Cost / Consequence |
|---|---|
| **Manual review burden** | Legal team spends 10–30 min per spurious flag; 100 FPs/month = 16–50 billable hours/month |
| **Deal velocity** | Vendor/counterparty frustration at repeated re-explanations; 2–5 day delays per contract |
| **Vendor relations** | Erosion of trust; risk that vendor escalates to customer (reputational) |
| **False confidence** | Over-flagging diminishes legal team''s trust in AI; may be ignored or cause alert fatigue |

### 2.3 Acceptable False Positive Rate
- **Target:** <10% of all AI flags are spurious  
- **Action threshold:** If FP rate exceeds 15% in any contract type, trigger model retraining or confidence-score recalibration

---

## 3. Acceptable Error Rates & Thresholds

### 3.1 False Negative Rate by Contract Type

| Contract Type | Target FN Rate | Rationale | Sampling Strategy |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Data Processing / DPA** | <2% | Regulatory criticality; GDPR penalties are severe | 100% human legal review; AI as secondary flag |
| **High-value ($>500k) contracts** | <5% | Financial exposure warrants high scrutiny | 100% legal review; AI flags prioritized |
| **Vendor MSA / IP** | <5% | Long-term strategic risk | 100% legal review |
| **SaaS / Standard Terms** | <10% | Lower financial/regulatory risk; higher volume | 100% legal review for contracts >$100k; 25% sampling for <$100k |
| **Service Level / SOW** | <10% | Medium risk; usually shorter duration | 100% legal review for >$250k; 50% sampling for <$250k |

### 3.2 False Positive Rate
- **Target across all types:** <10%  
- **Trigger for retraining:** >15% in any single contract type

### 3.3 Severity Thresholds for Escalation

| Severity | Criteria | Action |
|---|---|---|
| **Critical** | FN would expose org to >$500k loss OR regulatory fine | Halt deployment; escalate to Chief Legal; require 100% manual review |
| **High** | FN exposure $100k–$500k OR material compliance gap | Legal team co-review; confidence score must be >90% for AI flag |
| **Medium** | FN exposure $50k–$100k; operational impact | Legal team spot-check; AI flags marked for follow-up |
| **Low** | FN exposure <$50k; operational inconvenience | AI flag accepted without secondary review if confidence >85% |

---

## 4. Mitigating Controls Mapped to Each Scenario

### 4.1 Mitigating False Negatives

| Scenario | Mitigation Control | Owner | Frequency |
|---|---|---|---|
| **DPA/Data Processing contracts** | Human legal review (100%); AI as secondary flag only | Legal Team Lead | Per contract |
| **High-value contracts** | Mandatory dual-review: AI flag + senior attorney sign-off | Rule Set Owner + Senior Legal Counsel | Per contract |
| **Auto-renewal & liability caps** | Maintain AI rule set with updated market-standard language; quarterly refresh | Rule Set Owner | Quarterly |
| **IP assignment clauses** | Create domain-specific training data; tag all derivatives/improvements language | Rule Set Owner + Legal | Upon contract type expansion |
| **Missed clauses (post-incident)** | Root-cause analysis; retrain model; add synthetic examples | Rule Set Owner + Data Science | Within 5 days of discovery |
| **Volume sampling (SaaS <$100k)** | Random 25% manual audit of AI "pass" cases | Legal Team Lead | Monthly |

### 4.2 Mitigating False Positives

| Scenario | Mitigation Control | Owner | Frequency |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Model retraining** | If FP rate >15%, retrain with recent market-standard contracts | Rule Set Owner + Data Science | On-trigger or annually |
| **Confidence score calibration** | Adjust thresholds so only flags >X% confidence are shown to legal | Rule Set Owner | Quarterly |
| **Vendor feedback loop** | Collect vendor push-back on flags; document as false positives | Contract Manager | Per instance, aggregated quarterly |
| **Alert fatigue prevention** | If FP increases >10%, reduce flag volume or increase confidence threshold | Rule Set Owner | Quarterly review |

---

## 5. Annual Review & Update Plan

### 5.1 Review Process
- **Triggering event:** Annual review (by [TODO: INSERT_DATE]); OR material system change (new contract type, regulatory change, model update)
- **Data collection (60 days prior):** Gather FN/FP metrics, missed-clause incidents, vendor feedback, regulatory changes
- **Review meeting:** Rule Set Owner + Legal Team Lead + [TODO: INSERT_DATA_SCIENCE_LEAD] + AI Inventory sponsor
- **Outputs:**
  - Updated impact matrix (if market conditions shift)
  - Revised acceptable error rates
  - New or modified mitigating controls
  - Model retraining roadmap (if needed)
  - Jira ticket(s) for action items

### 5.2 Material Change Triggers
Update within 30 days if:
- New regulatory requirement (e.g., AI Act article affecting contract review)
- Incident: FN causes >$250k loss or regulatory fine
- Contract volume or types expand significantly
- AI model version upgrade or retraining
- Vendor/counterparty feedback indicates persistent FP issue

---

## 6. Sign-Off & Accountability

| Role | Name | Signature | Date |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rule Set Owner (AI/Contract Review) | [TODO: INSERT_NAME] | | [TODO: INSERT_DATE] |
| Legal Team Lead | [TODO: INSERT_NAME] | | [TODO: INSERT_DATE] |
| AI Inventory Sponsor / CISO | [TODO: INSERT_NAME] | | [TODO: INSERT_DATE] |

---

## 7. Appendix: Related Documents
- **AI Inventory Epic:** [TODO: INSERT_JIRA_EPIC_URL]
- **Contract Review AI Model Card:** [TODO: INSERT_LINK]
- **Acceptable Use Policy:** [TODO: INSERT_LINK]
- **Incident Response Runbook:** [TODO: INSERT_LINK]
