INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('a4535d84-c4d4-4fab-b502-287e43d29996', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '655e2baa-9a21-4e1b-8449-d9f8202770a7', 10, 'Implement a kill switch that allows the named HR or security first responder to disable the copilot for all users within 15 minutes, without requiring developer intervention, while preserving all logs and in-progress session data.', 'If the copilot is generating biased or legally deficient drafts at scale — or a data boundary failure is discovered — every additional interaction compounds the damage; rapid disablement is essential given drafts auto-save to HRIS.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-12T05:43:16.455547+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 14 (human oversight — ability to stop); Art. 9 (risk management — corrective actions)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.8","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 4.1; MANAGE 4.3"}'::jsonb, 'Implement the kill switch as one of: (1) In Entra ID, create a Conditional Access policy ''HR-Copilot-Emergency-Block'' in report-only mode; the first responder switches it to enforce mode to block all access to the copilot Enterprise Application — requires only Entra ID Conditional Access Administrator role; (2) Alternatively, in the Azure OpenAI resource, disable the deployment endpoint via Azure Portal or CLI (''az cognitiveservices account deployment delete''). Grant the named first responder the minimum Entra ID role required for the chosen mechanism. Document the steps in the incident runbook. Test quarterly and log the test with execution time.', 'Documented kill switch procedure with the specific Azure or application mechanism identified; access granted to named first responders; test execution log showing disablement completed within 15 minutes.', 'Execute the kill switch procedure in a test environment; measure time from initiation to confirmed user-facing unavailability; verify logs are preserved and no data loss occurs.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'runbook', 'markdown', 'hr-copilot-kill-switch-runbook.md', '<!-- Control: a4535d84-c4d4-4fab-b502-287e43d29996 — HR Copilot Kill Switch Runbook -->
<!-- Pillar 10 | SCAFFOLD — review all TODOs before publishing as an operational runbook -->

# HR Copilot — Emergency Kill Switch Runbook

## Purpose
Allow a **named HR or Security First Responder** to fully disable the HR Copilot for all users within **15 minutes**, without developer intervention, while preserving all logs and in-progress session data.

---

## 1. Named First Responders

| Role | Name | Entra UPN | Backup Contact |
|------|------|-----------|----------------|
| HR Lead | <!-- TODO: insert name --> | <!-- TODO: demo@community.example --> | <!-- TODO: backup --> |
| Security Analyst | <!-- TODO: insert name --> | <!-- TODO: demo@community.example --> | <!-- TODO: backup --> |

> **TODO:** Populate this table and store it in the Security team''s shared channel in Teams and in the OneTrust GRC incident register.

---

## 2. Prerequisites — Roles Granted in Advance

Before an incident occurs, ensure the following is in place:

### Mechanism A — Entra ID Conditional Access Block (Preferred)
- First Responder is assigned the **Conditional Access Administrator** Entra ID role (or a PIM-eligible activation of it).
  - `TODO: Assign via Entra ID > Roles and administrators > Conditional Access Administrator`
- A Conditional Access policy named **`HR-Copilot-Emergency-Block`** exists in **Report-only** mode targeting the HR Copilot Enterprise Application.
  - `TODO: See Section 3 for policy details.`

### Mechanism B — Azure OpenAI Deployment Disable (Fallback)
- First Responder is assigned **Cognitive Services Contributor** (or a custom role scoped to the HR Copilot deployment resource only) on the Azure OpenAI resource.
  - `TODO: Resource group: <rg-name>; Subscription: <subscription-id>`
- Azure CLI access confirmed and tested.

---

## 3. Conditional Access Policy Specification — `HR-Copilot-Emergency-Block`

> This policy must be created in Entra ID **before** any incident. It sits in **Report-only** mode at rest and is switched to **Enabled** during an incident.

```
Policy Name:    HR-Copilot-Emergency-Block
State:          Report-only  ← normal operating state
Target users:   All users  (or scope to HR Copilot security group if preferred)
                TODO: group name = <HR-Copilot-Users-SG>
Target app:     <HR Copilot Enterprise Application Object ID>
                TODO: App display name = <HR Copilot App Name>
Conditions:     None (block applies universally)
Grant controls: Block access
Session:        (none)
```

> **TODO:** Create this policy via Entra ID > Security > Conditional Access > New policy. Validate in Report-only mode during quarterly test (Section 7).

---

## 4. Kill Switch Activation — Step-by-Step (Target: ≤ 15 minutes)

### MECHANISM A — Entra ID Conditional Access (Primary)

**Estimated time: 3–5 minutes**

1. **Receive incident trigger** (alert from Sentinel/Splunk, peer escalation, or own discovery).
2. Open [https://entra.microsoft.com](https://entra.microsoft.com) and sign in with your First Responder account.
   - If PIM-eligible: activate **Conditional Access Administrator** role first (allow 1–2 min for activation).
   - `TODO: PIM activation link: https://entra.microsoft.com/#view/Microsoft_Azure_PIMCommon/...`
3. Navigate to **Protection → Conditional Access → Policies**.
4. Locate policy **`HR-Copilot-Emergency-Block`**.
5. Click the policy → set **Enable policy** to **`On`** → click **Save**.
6. Confirm policy state shows **Enabled** in the policy list.
7. **Verify**: Ask a test account (non-production user) to attempt access to the HR Copilot app — confirm they receive an access-blocked message within 60 seconds.
8. **Log the action** (see Section 6).

---

### MECHANISM B — Azure OpenAI Deployment Disable (Fallback if Mechanism A unavailable)

**Estimated time: 5–10 minutes**

> ⚠️ Use only if Mechanism A cannot be activated. This disables the model endpoint directly.

1. Open Azure Cloud Shell or a local terminal with Azure CLI installed and authenticated.
2. Run:
```bash
# TODO: Replace all placeholder values before use
az login  # skip if already authenticated

# Confirm current deployment state
az cognitiveservices account deployment show \
  --name "<azure-openai-resource-name>" \
  --resource-group "<resource-group-name>" \
  --deployment-name "<hr-copilot-deployment-name>"  # TODO: e.g. hr-copilot-gpt4

# DISABLE: Delete the deployment to block all inference calls
# WARNING: This terminates the deployment. Re-deployment requires developer action.
# Logs and data are NOT deleted by this command.
az cognitiveservices account deployment delete \
  --name "<azure-openai-resource-name>" \
  --resource-group "<resource-group-name>" \
  --deployment-name "<hr-copilot-deployment-name>" \
  --yes
```
3. Confirm the deployment no longer appears in:
   - Azure Portal → Azure OpenAI resource → Deployments
4. **Log the action** (see Section 6).

> **Note on data preservation:** Neither mechanism deletes logs. Azure OpenAI diagnostic logs continue to flow to Log Analytics / Sentinel. SharePoint/Workday session data persists independently. Confirm with your data team that no in-progress sessions auto-purge on disconnect. `TODO: verify session persistence with HR platform owner.`

---

## 5. Escalation & Communication

| Step | Action | Owner | Tool |
|------|--------|-------|------|
| T+0 | Trigger kill switch | First Responder | Entra ID / Azure CLI |
| T+5 | Notify CISO / HR Director | First Responder | Teams — `#security-incidents` channel |
| T+10 | Open P1 incident ticket | First Responder | HR Service Delivery (ITSM) |
| T+15 | Confirm all users blocked | Security Analyst | Sentinel / Splunk sign-in logs |
| T+30 | Initial impact assessment | Security + HR | Teams war room |
| T+60 | Executive briefing | CISO | <!-- TODO: define channel --> |

> **TODO:** Pre-create a Teams channel `#hr-copilot-incident-war-room` with the relevant stakeholders pre-added.

