INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('3e348dcf-ec5e-4b96-baa0-7b86fa86090f', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '97cd8230-e2e2-47e4-944a-e5896b5ef796', 1, 'Maintain a living inventory record for the contract review AI system that includes data sources, model provider, integration points (DocuSign, OpenAI API, AWS Bedrock), decision scope, named owners, and current risk tier with escalation triggers documented.', 'Without a single authoritative record, no one can verify what the system sees, does, or who is accountable — and the confirmed escalation triggers (T1, T3 already met) make accurate classification critical.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-10T03:46:26.461699+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9 (risk management system); Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.5.2; A.5.4; A.6.1.2","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 1.1; GOVERN 1.2; MAP 1.1"}'::jsonb, 'Create a Jira Epic or Confluence page as the AI inventory record. Include fields: system name, business owner (Legal team lead), technical owner, AI provider (OpenAI API via AWS Bedrock), integrations (DocuSign API), data classification (Confidential), risk tier (3), escalation triggers (T1–T6 from risk assessment). Tag with label ''ai-inventory'' for queryability. Set a quarterly review reminder assigned to the business owner.', 'Inventory entry in a central register (e.g., Confluence page or CMDB record) showing system name, business owner (Legal team), technical owner, data classification (Confidential), model provider (OpenAI API), integrations (DocuSign), risk tier (3 — pending re-evaluation given escalation triggers), and last review date.', 'Pull the inventory record and verify every field is populated, current, and matches the live system configuration; confirm the escalation triggers from the risk assessment are documented and have named monitors.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'runbook', 'markdown', 'ai-inventory-setup.md', '# Control 3e348dcf-ec5e-4b96-baa0-7b86fa86090f: AI System Living Inventory Record

This runbook establishes a living inventory record for the contract review AI system in Jira and Confluence.
No code deployment required — this is a manual setup and governance process.

## Objective

Create and maintain a single authoritative source of truth documenting the contract review AI system''s:
- Data sources and classification
- Model provider and integration endpoints
- Decision scope and escalation triggers
- Named owners and accountability
- Current risk tier and review cadence

## Prerequisites

- Access to Jira (Enterprise or Cloud)
- Access to Confluence (linked to the same organization)
- Identified business owner (Legal team lead) and technical owner
- Risk assessment document confirming T1, T3 trigger status

## Setup Steps

### 1. Create Jira Epic for AI System Inventory

1. In Jira, navigate to **Projects** → **[Your AI Governance Project]**
   - *TODO: Replace with your actual Jira project key (e.g., `AIGOV`)*
2. Click **Create** → **Epic**
3. Populate the following fields:
   - **Epic Name:** `Contract Review AI System Inventory`
   - **Epic Link:** Link to Confluence page (created in step 2)
   - **Labels:** `ai-inventory`, `contract-review`, `prod`
   - **Description:**
     ```
     Authoritative inventory record for the contract review AI system.
     Tracks data sources, model integrations, risk tier, owners, and escalation triggers.
     See linked Confluence page for detailed specification.
     Review quarterly or when system scope changes.
     ```

### 2. Create Confluence Page: AI System Specification

1. In Confluence, navigate to **[Your AI Governance Space]**
   - *TODO: Replace with your Confluence space key*
2. Click **Create** → **Page**
3. Title: `Contract Review AI System — Living Inventory`
4. Populate the following template:

```
# Contract Review AI System — Living Inventory

**Last Updated:** [TODAY''S DATE]
**Next Review Due:** [QUARTERLY DATE]
**Status:** Active

## System Overview

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **System Name** | Contract Review AI |
| **Business Owner** | [Legal Team Lead Name] — [Email] — [Phone] |
| **Technical Owner** | [Platform/AI Engineer Name] — [Email] — [Phone] |
| **System Purpose** | Analyze and summarize contract documents for legal review |
| **Data Classification** | Confidential |
| **Current Risk Tier** | 3 |
| **Operational Status** | Production |

## Model & Provider

- **Primary AI Provider:** OpenAI API (accessed via AWS Bedrock integration)
- **Model:** [TODO: Specify model version, e.g., `gpt-4-turbo`] |
- **AWS Region:** [TODO: Specify AWS region where Bedrock is deployed] |
- **Bedrock Model ARN:** `arn:aws:bedrock:[region]:[account-id]:model/anthropic.claude-v2` or equivalent [TODO: Confirm actual ARN] |

## Data Sources & Integration Points

| Integration | Data Flowing | Classification | Owner |
|-------------|--------------|-----------------|-------|
| **DocuSign API** | Contract documents (PDFs, JSON metadata) | Confidential | Legal Ops |
| **OpenAI API via AWS Bedrock** | Contract text (for inference only) | Confidential | Platform |
| **Internal Contract DB** | [TODO: Name of system] | Confidential | [Owner] |
| **Output Storage** | Summary + risk flags (S3 bucket [TODO: bucket name]) | Confidential | Platform |

## Decision Scope

The system is authorized to:
- Ingest contract documents from DocuSign
- Extract and summarize key contract terms
- Flag potential risk clauses (payment terms, liability, term length, IP ownership)
- Return a structured summary to the legal review interface

The system is **NOT** authorized to:
- Execute or approve contracts
- Modify contract documents
- Access non-contract confidential data
- Interact with external systems outside DocuSign, Bedrock, and internal DB

## Risk Assessment & Escalation Triggers

**Baseline Risk Tier:** 3 (Medium-High)

**Confirmed Escalation Triggers:**
- **T1 (Triggered):** System processes contracts with deal size >$[TODO: threshold]M
- **T3 (Triggered):** System outputs used in deals with >3 counter-parties
- **T2:** System processes contracts with non-standard liability or IP clauses
- **T4:** Model accuracy drops below [TODO: specify %] on validation set
- **T5:** Unauthorized access attempt to contract data or model inference API
- **T6:** More than 2 business exceptions to decision rules within 30 days

**Action on Trigger:**
When any trigger fires, the business owner and technical owner must:
1. Create a Jira incident in [TODO: incident project]
2. Escalate to [TODO: stakeholder names/group]
3. Document root cause and remediation within 5 business days
4. Re-assess risk tier if scope or model changes

## Quarterly Review Cadence

- **Owner:** Business Owner (Legal Team Lead)
- **Frequency:** Every Q (e.g., Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4)
- **Checklist:**
  - [ ] Verify no unauthorized integrations or data flows
  - [ ] Review escalation trigger status (any new activations?)
  - [ ] Confirm model version and Bedrock endpoint are current
  - [ ] Check access logs for anomalies
  - [ ] Validate risk tier remains appropriate
  - [ ] Update this page with latest metadata
  - [ ] Confirm owners are still in role

- **Jira Reminder:** Create a recurring Jira task (or use automation rule) to email business owner 2 weeks before each quarter end, titled:
  ```
  [ACTION] Contract Review AI System — Q[N] Inventory Review Due
  ```

## Related Documents

- Risk Assessment Report: [Link to risk assessment]
- Data Handling Policy: [Link to policy]
- Incident Log: [Link to incidents related to this system]
- Model Performance Dashboard: [Link to monitoring dashboard]

---

**Version History:**
| Date | Author | Change |
|------|--------|--------|
| [TODAY] | [Your Name] | Initial inventory record created |
```

### 3. Create Jira Automation Rule for Quarterly Reminders

1. In Jira, go to **Projects** → **Project Settings** → **Automation**
2. Click **Create Rule**
3. Configure:
   - **Trigger:** Scheduled (Quarterly)
     - Cron: `0 9 1 1,4,7,10 *` (First Monday of Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4)
   - **Condition:** None (always run)
   - **Action:** Send Email
     - **To:** Business Owner (Legal Team Lead)
       - *TODO: Insert actual email address*
     - **Subject:** `[ACTION] Contract Review AI System — Q[N] Inventory Review Due`
     - **Body:**
       ```
       Hi [Business Owner Name],
       
       It''s time for your quarterly review of the Contract Review AI System.
       
       Please verify the living inventory record in Confluence:
       [Link to Confluence page]
       
       Checklist:
       - System scope unchanged?
       - Risk tier still accurate?
       - All owners still in role?
       - Any new escalation triggers?
       
       Reply in Jira when complete: [Link to Epic]
       ```

### 4. Link Epic to Other AI Governance Records

1. In the Jira Epic, add links to:
   - Related incidents or risks
   - Model monitoring dashboards
   - Data classification policy
   - Approval chain for scope changes
2. Apply labels: `ai-inventory`, `contract-review`, `prod`, `legal`

## Validation Checklist

Before marking this control complete:

- [ ] Confluence page created with all required fields populated
- [ ] Jira Epic created and linked to Confluence page
- [ ] Business owner and technical owner identified and notified
- [ ] Escalation triggers (T1–T6) documented with action procedures
- [ ] Quarterly reminder automation rule configured in Jira
- [ ] AI System Inventory labeled with `ai-inventory` tag
- [ ] First quarterly review scheduled on calendar
- [ ] Access restricted so only relevant stakeholders can edit (use Confluence space permissions)

## Ongoing Maintenance

- **When system scope changes:** Update Confluence page within 2 business days; create a Jira issue to track the change
- **When escalation trigger fires:** Create Jira incident linked to this inventory record
- **Quarterly:** Complete the review checklist; update "Last Updated" timestamp
- **When owners change:** Update Confluence page and re-assign Jira automation reminder

---

