<!-- Pillar 7 | Required — REVIEW-BEFORE-APPLY SCAFFOLD. Adapt to your copilot/review UI implementation before deploying. -->

# Human Review Panel — Grounding Context Requirements

## Purpose
Ensure that every human reviewer in the HR AI copilot approval workflow is presented with the **full evidentiary context** — not just the polished AI-generated draft — so that the review step constitutes a genuine quality gate rather than a rubber-stamp.

---

## Scope
- **System:** HR AI Copilot built on Azure OpenAI Service + Azure AI Search
- **Review surface:** Copilot review UI (Teams Adaptive Card, SharePoint-embedded app, or HR Service Delivery portal — see TODO below)
- **Reviewers:** HR practitioners, HR managers, or designated approvers in Entra ID reviewer group
- **Trigger:** Any AI-drafted HR communication, policy response, or case resolution that enters the approval queue

---

## Required Review Context Payload

The backend API that serves the review screen **MUST** assemble and return the following fields for every pending review item. These fields are sourced at generation time and stored alongside the draft.

| Field | Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `original_user_prompt` | User input captured at request time | Verbatim; do not summarise |
| `retrieved_documents[]` | Azure AI Search response | See schema below |
| `grounding_confidence_score` | Similarity threshold check post-retrieval | Float 0–1; flag if below threshold |
| `output_validation_flags[]` | Output validation layer | See schema below |
| `draft_content` | Azure OpenAI generation | Editable by reviewer |
| `review_deadline` | Workflow SLA | ISO-8601 timestamp |

### `retrieved_documents[]` schema (per document)
```json
{
  "document_id": "<Azure AI Search document key>",
  "title": "<document title or filename>",
  "source_url": "<SharePoint Online or storage URL>",   // TODO: confirm URL pattern for your tenant
  "relevance_score": 0.87,                              // @search.score from Azure AI Search
  "snippet_preview": "<first ~300 chars of the matched passage>"
}
```

### `output_validation_flags[]` schema (per flag)
```json
{
  "flag_id": "PII_DETECTED",         // e.g. PII_DETECTED | POLICY_TERM_MISSING | LOW_CONFIDENCE | SENSITIVE_LABEL
  "severity": "HIGH",                // HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
  "triggering_pattern": "<regex or rule identifier that fired>",
  "matched_excerpt": "<excerpt from draft that triggered the flag>"
}
```

---

## UI Layout Specification

### Layout
Implement a **split-pane layout** within the review screen:

```
┌─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐
│  LEFT / TOP PANE            │  RIGHT / BOTTOM PANE             │
│  ─────────────────          │  ─────────────────               │
│  Editable Draft             │  Review Context  [NON-COLLAPSIBLE]│
│                             │                                  │
│  [Draft text area]          │  1. Original User Prompt         │
│                             │  2. Retrieved Source Documents   │
│                             │     • Title + relevance score    │
│  [Approve] [Request Changes]│     • Snippet preview            │
│  [Escalate]                 │     • Source URL link            │
│                             │  3. Grounding Confidence Score   │
│                             │  4. Output Validation Flags      │
└─────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Non-Collapsibility Requirement
- The **Review Context pane MUST NOT** be collapsible, minimisable, or dismissible during the active approval flow.
- The **Approve / Submit** action button MUST be rendered **below** all Review Context sections in DOM order (or require explicit scroll-past acknowledgement), so reviewers cannot approve without encountering the evidence.
- Implement a scroll-gate: track `reviewContextScrolled = true` client-side; the Approve button remains `disabled` until this flag is set.

> **TODO:** Implement `reviewContextScrolled` tracking in your front-end framework (React, SPFx, Teams JS SDK, or Power Apps — whichever hosts the review UI). Verify this cannot be bypassed via keyboard shortcuts or direct API calls.

### Visual Treatment for Flags and Low Confidence
- If `grounding_confidence_score < 0.70` (TODO: align threshold with your similarity cutoff), display a **⚠ Low Confidence** banner in amber at the top of the Review Context pane.
- Each `output_validation_flag` with `severity = HIGH` must display a **🔴 red callout block** pinned above the draft pane.
- Each `severity = MEDIUM` flag renders as a **🟡 yellow inline annotation**.

---

## Backend Implementation Checklist

- [ ] **Capture at generation time:** Store `original_user_prompt`, `retrieved_documents[]`, `grounding_confidence_score`, and `output_validation_flags[]` atomically with the draft in the review queue data store.
  - > **TODO:** Identify your review queue store (e.g., Azure SQL, Dataverse, SharePoint List, HR Service Delivery record) and add these fields to its schema.
- [ ] **API endpoint:** Expose a `GET /review-items/{id}/context` endpoint (or equivalent) that returns the full payload above. Protect with Entra ID authentication; scope to the reviewer''s group.
  - > **TODO:** Register the API app in Entra ID, define the required API permission scope (e.g., `HRCopilot.Review.Read`), and restrict to the HR reviewer security group (Object ID: TODO).
- [ ] **Immutability:** The context payload must be read-only to reviewers. Only the `draft_content` field may be edited.
- [ ] **Audit log:** On approval or rejection, write an audit record to Purview Information Protection / unified audit log containing: reviewer UPN, review item ID, action taken, timestamp, and whether any HIGH flags were present at time of approval.
  - > **TODO:** Configure Purview audit log retention for HR AI review events to meet your data retention policy (minimum 1 year recommended).
- [ ] **Timeout/expiry:** If a review item is not actioned within the SLA window (TODO: define SLA, e.g., 24 h), auto-escalate to secondary reviewer and log the event to Microsoft Sentinel.

---

## Entra ID — Reviewer Group Configuration

```
# TODO: Create or confirm the Entra ID security group for HR AI reviewers
# Group name example: sg-hr-ai-copilot-reviewers
# Assign this group as the required approver role in your HR Service Delivery workflow
# Apply Conditional Access policy requiring MFA for members of this group
# TODO: Set group owner and review cadence in Entra ID Access Reviews (quarterly recommended)
```

---

## Operational Procedures

### New Reviewer Onboarding
1. Add reviewer to `sg-hr-ai-copilot-reviewers` Entra ID group (requires manager approval).
2. Complete the **HR AI Review Training** module (TODO: create and link module in your LMS).
3. Training must cover: how to interpret relevance scores, what each flag type means, when to escalate vs. reject.
4. Document completion in HR Service Delivery onboarding ticket.

### Review Quality Spot-Check (Monthly)
1. HR AI System Owner samples 5% of approved items from the previous month.
2. Verify that at least one HIGH-flag item per week resulted in a non-approval action (edit or rejection). If 100% of HIGH-flag items are approved unchanged, trigger a reviewer calibration session.
3. Log spot-check results in OneTrust GRC as evidence against this control.

### Escalation Path
| Condition | Action |
|---|---|
| Reviewer cannot interpret a flag | Escalate to HR AI System Owner via HR Service Delivery ticket |
| Grounding score < 0.50 | Do not approve; return to requester with explanation |
| PII detected in draft intended for broad distribution | Escalate to Purview/DLP team before approval |
| Suspected prompt injection in original user prompt | Raise security incident; do not approve; notify Security Operations |

---

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Review UI renders all four context elements (prompt, documents, confidence, flags) for every pending item.
- [ ] Review Context pane cannot be collapsed or bypassed; Approve button is disabled until scroll-gate is satisfied.
- [ ] Approval actions are written to the Purview audit log within 60 seconds.
- [ ] At least one end-to-end test with a LOW confidence item and a HIGH flag item passes UAT before go-live.
- [ ] Spot-check procedure is scheduled in OneTrust GRC as a recurring monthly task.

---

