<!-- Scaffold only. Review all TODO items with HR Leadership, Legal, and Compliance before publishing. -->

# Employee Relations AI Decision Ownership Matrix — Runbook

## Purpose
This runbook defines the process for establishing, maintaining, and operationalising a **named decision owner** for each high-risk Employee Relations (ER) action category where an AI-generated draft (Azure OpenAI / HR Copilot) may be presented to an HR practitioner. It ensures that no AI output becomes a de facto decision in the absence of clearly accountable human review.

---

## 1. Scope

Applies to all ER actions processed through the HR Service Delivery platform and/or the Azure OpenAI–backed HR Copilot where outputs are used to inform:

| Action Category | Risk Level |
|---|---|
| Discipline (written warning, PIP initiation) | High |
| Termination (involuntary, for cause, redundancy) | High |
| Accommodation (disability, religious, family) | High |
| Grievance Resolution | High |
| Performance Outcomes (rating finalisation, demotion) | High |

---

## 2. Decision Ownership Matrix

> **TODO:** Populate every cell below with actual named roles and individuals. Obtain sign-off from HR Leadership and Legal before publishing to SharePoint Online.

| Action Category | Decision Owner Role | Backup / Escalation Role | Regional / BU Scope | Named Individual (Review Cycle) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Discipline | Senior ER Specialist | HR Director — [BU] | [Region / BU — TODO] | [Name — TODO; review annually] |
| Termination | HR Director — [BU] | Chief People Officer | [Region / BU — TODO] | [Name — TODO; review annually] |
| Accommodation | Senior ER Specialist (ADA/reasonable adjustment lead) | Legal Counsel — Employment | [Region / BU — TODO] | [Name — TODO; review annually] |
| Grievance Resolution | Senior ER Specialist | HR Director — [BU] | [Region / BU — TODO] | [Name — TODO; review annually] |
| Performance Outcomes | HR Business Partner (Level ≥ Senior) | HR Director — [BU] | [Region / BU — TODO] | [Name — TODO; review annually] |

### 2.1 Matrix Maintenance Rules
- The matrix **must be updated within 5 business days** of any named individual leaving the role.
- A review is mandatory at each annual AI inventory audit (see Section 5).
- Interim cover must be assigned (and documented) before the named individual goes on extended leave.

---

## 3. SharePoint Online Publication

1. **Create the document library** (if not already present):
   - Site: `https://[tenant].sharepoint.com/sites/HRPolicy` <!-- TODO: replace [tenant] with your M365 tenant name -->
   - Library: `ER Decision Ownership`
   - Folder: `AI Governance`
2. **Upload this matrix** as `ER_Decision_Ownership_Matrix_v[VERSION]_[DATE].xlsx` (maintain versioned copies; do not delete prior versions).
3. **Set permissions**:
   - Read: All HR Staff (Entra ID group `GRP-HR-All`) <!-- TODO: confirm group name -->
   - Edit: HR Governance team (Entra ID group `GRP-HR-Governance`) <!-- TODO: confirm group name -->
   - No external sharing.
4. **Pin the document** in the HR Copilot SharePoint site and in the relevant Teams channel (`HR ER Governance`). <!-- TODO: confirm Teams channel name -->
5. Apply a **Purview Information Protection sensitivity label** of `Confidential – HR` to the document. <!-- TODO: confirm label name in your Purview tenant -->

---

## 4. OneTrust AI Inventory Linkage

1. Open the OneTrust GRC & Security Assurance Cloud console.
2. Navigate to **AI Inventory** → locate the HR Copilot / Azure OpenAI ER assistant record. <!-- TODO: confirm the exact inventory record name -->
3. In the record''s **Controls & Evidence** section, attach:
   - A hyperlink to the SharePoint document (Section 3 above).
   - The date of last review.
   - The name of the HR Governance owner responsible for the matrix.
4. Set a **recurring task** in OneTrust for annual review, assigned to the HR Governance owner.
5. Tag the inventory record with the risk attribute `High-Risk ER Actions — Decision Ownership`.

---

## 5. Copilot UI Integration Requirements

When the HR Copilot (Azure OpenAI Service) triggers an **output validation flag** or an **escalation threshold** for any of the five high-risk categories, the application **must** surface the following in the user interface before the practitioner can proceed:

```
⚠️  ESCALATION REQUIRED — [Action Category]

This AI-generated draft requires independent human review by the named
Decision Owner before any action is taken.

Decision Owner:   [Role Name]  —  [Named Individual]
Contact:          [Email] | [Teams handle]
Escalation ID:   [Auto-generated case reference]

You must confirm that you have independently evaluated the underlying
facts and that the AI output does not reflect the sole basis for this
decision before submitting.

[ ] I confirm I have independently reviewed the facts.   [Submit]  [Cancel]
```

> **TODO (Engineering):** Implement the above prompt block in the Copilot application layer. Pull Decision Owner data dynamically from the SharePoint list (use Microsoft Graph API with app registration scoped to `Sites.Read.All` on the ER governance site only). Cache with a TTL of ≤ 4 hours to ensure near-real-time accuracy on personnel changes.

> **TODO (Engineering):** Log every escalation acknowledgement (user UPN, timestamp, case reference, action category, Decision Owner displayed) to a dedicated Azure Monitor / Log Analytics workspace for audit purposes. Forward to Microsoft Sentinel for anomaly detection.

---

## 6. Decision Owner Obligations

Each named Decision Owner must, **before approving any AI-assisted ER action**:

1. **Independently read the source documents** (Workday HCM case file, HR Service Delivery ticket, supporting evidence) — not solely the AI-generated summary.
2. **Verify completeness**: Confirm the AI draft does not omit material facts (e.g., mitigating circumstances, prior commitments, protected characteristic indicators).
3. **Apply independent judgement**: The AI output is an input, not a recommendation to rubber-stamp.
4. **Record rationale**: Document their independent review rationale in the HR Service Delivery case record (free-text field `Decision Owner Notes`). <!-- TODO: confirm field name -->
5. **Escalate further** if legal risk is identified (e.g., potential discrimination claim) — see backup/escalation roles in the matrix.

---

## 7. Training & Attestation

- All named Decision Owners must complete the **AI-Assisted HR Decision-Making** training module before being listed on the matrix. <!-- TODO: confirm LMS module name and link -->
- Annual re-attestation required; tracked in OneTrust.
- Training records stored in Workday HCM Learning. <!-- TODO: confirm Workday module -->

---

## 8. Audit & Review Cadence

| Activity | Frequency | Owner | Evidence Location |
|---|---|---|---|
| Matrix accuracy review | Annual (+ on personnel change) | HR Governance Lead | SharePoint ER Decision Ownership library |
| OneTrust AI inventory review | Annual | HR Governance Lead + GRC team | OneTrust AI Inventory record |
| Copilot escalation log review | Quarterly | Senior ER Specialist | Azure Monitor / Sentinel |
| Decision Owner training attestation | Annual | HR L&D + GRC team | Workday HCM / OneTrust |

---

