# DPIA & EU AI Act High-Risk Classification Runbook
## HR AI Use Case — Azure OpenAI Service (Employment, Workers Management)

---

## 1. Purpose & Scope

This runbook guides the DPO, Privacy team, and AI governance owner through:
1. Formally classifying the HR AI use case as **EU AI Act Annex III, Area 4 — Employment / Workers Management** (high-risk).
2. Completing and maintaining a **GDPR Article 35 Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA)** in **OneTrust GRC & Privacy Management**.

**In-scope systems:** Workday HCM · HR Service Delivery · SharePoint Online · Microsoft Teams · Azure OpenAI Service · Azure AI Search · Purview Information Protection · Entra ID

---

## 2. EU AI Act High-Risk Classification

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Annex III Area | **4 — Employment, workers management, access to self-employment** |
| Classification | **High-Risk AI System** |
| Rationale | System processes employee personal data (including sensitive categories) to assist HR decisions on case management, investigation, and workforce queries — directly within scope of Art. 6(2) and Annex III(4). |
| Classification Owner | TODO: `<AI Governance Owner name/role>` |
| Review Cadence | Annually or on material system change |

**Action:** Record this classification in the OneTrust AI Governance module (or equivalent register) and link it to the DPIA record created in Step 3.

---

## 3. DPIA — OneTrust Setup Steps

### 3.1 Create / Update the DPIA Record

1. Log in to **OneTrust Privacy Management**.
2. Navigate to **Privacy Program → Data Protection Impact Assessments**.
3. Click **New Assessment** → select template: `DPIA (GDPR Art. 35)`.  
   - TODO: Confirm your organisation''s OneTrust DPIA template name.
4. Title: `DPIA — HR AI Case Management (Azure OpenAI) — v<VERSION> — <YYYY-MM-DD>`
5. Link to the **Processing Activity** record for HR case management / HRIS in OneTrust''s Data Inventory.
   - TODO: Confirm the existing processing activity record ID/name in OneTrust.

### 3.2 Data Element Mapping

Document each data element, its source system, and data flow destination:

| Data Element | Source System | Destination | Special Category? (Art. 9) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Employee full name | Workday HCM | Azure OpenAI Service | No |
| Job role / title | Workday HCM | Azure OpenAI Service | No |
| Work location | Workday HCM | Azure OpenAI Service | No |
| Tenure / employment dates | Workday HCM | Azure OpenAI Service | No |
| HR case notes | HR Service Delivery | Azure OpenAI Service | **Potentially yes** (health, union membership, disciplinary) |
| Investigation summaries | HR Service Delivery / SharePoint Online | Azure OpenAI Service | **Potentially yes** |
| HRIS records (pay band, absence) | Workday HCM | Azure AI Search (index) | No / Potentially yes |
| Identity & access context | Entra ID | Azure OpenAI / AI Search | No |

> **⚠ TODO:** Validate this table with HR, Legal, and the system owner. Confirm whether case notes may contain health data, trade union membership, or criminal records — these are Art. 9 special categories requiring explicit lawful basis.

### 3.3 Processing Purposes & Lawful Basis

Document each purpose in OneTrust:

| Purpose | Proposed Lawful Basis (GDPR Art. 6) | Art. 9 Basis (if applicable) |
|---|---|---|
| HR case triage and summarisation | Art. 6(1)(b) — Contract performance **or** Art. 6(1)(f) — Legitimate interests | Art. 9(2)(b) — Employment law obligation |
| Investigation assistance / RAG retrieval | Art. 6(1)(f) — Legitimate interests | Art. 9(2)(b) or Art. 9(2)(g) — substantial public interest |
| Workforce query answering | Art. 6(1)(b) — Contract | N/A |

> **TODO:** Confirm lawful basis with DPO. Legitimate interests requires a completed **LIA (Legitimate Interests Assessment)** — create a linked LIA record in OneTrust if this basis is selected.

### 3.4 Risk Assessment

Complete the risk section of the OneTrust DPIA template covering at minimum:

- [ ] **Data minimisation:** Are all fields sent to Azure OpenAI necessary? Document which fields are filtered before the prompt.
  - TODO: Confirm prompt construction logic with the AI engineering team; attach architecture diagram.
- [ ] **Sensitive category exposure:** Case notes flow unfiltered to Azure OpenAI Service — assess residual risk and document mitigating controls (Purview labels, network isolation, RBAC in Entra ID).
- [ ] **Profiling / automated decision-making:** Does the AI output directly influence an employment decision? If yes, document Art. 22 compliance (right to explanation, human review).
- [ ] **Data retention in Azure OpenAI:** Confirm Microsoft''s data retention window for prompt/completion logs (currently 30 days for abuse monitoring unless zero data retention is contracted).
  - TODO: Attach or link the **Microsoft Azure OpenAI Data Processing Addendum (DPA)** confirming no training on customer data. Download from: https://aka.ms/oai-dpa
- [ ] **Cross-border transfers:** Azure OpenAI region must be confirmed (EU region preferred). Document transfer mechanism (SCCs, adequacy decision).
  - TODO: Confirm Azure OpenAI deployment region — `<e.g., swedencentral, westeurope>` — and attach evidence.

### 3.5 Mitigation Controls to Document in DPIA

| Control | Implementation | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Entra ID RBAC — least-privilege access to AI endpoints | Terraform / Entra conditional access | TODO: `<Platform Eng team>` |
| Purview sensitivity labels on case note documents | Purview Information Protection policy | TODO: `<Data Governance team>` |
| Prompt filtering / PII redaction before Azure OpenAI | Application layer (pre-processing) | TODO: `<AI Dev team>` |
| Azure OpenAI content filtering enabled | Azure portal / Terraform | TODO: `<AI Ops team>` |
| Sentinel + Splunk monitoring for anomalous AI queries | Sentinel analytics rules | TODO: `<SecOps team>` |
| No training on customer data (contractual) | Microsoft Azure OpenAI DPA | DPO |
| Human-in-the-loop for consequential HR decisions | HR process / HRSD workflow | HR Director |

---

## 4. DPO Consultation & Approval Workflow (OneTrust)

1. Complete all sections of the DPIA record in OneTrust.
2. Set assessment status to **"Under Review"** and assign to DPO:  
   - TODO: `<DPO name / OneTrust user email>`
3. DPO reviews within **14 calendar days** (recommended).
4. If residual risk is **high and cannot be mitigated**, DPO must consult the supervisory authority (GDPR Art. 36) **before go-live**.
5. On approval, set status to **"Approved"** — record DPO sign-off date and approver in OneTrust.
6. Attach supporting evidence:
   - [ ] Microsoft Azure OpenAI DPA
   - [ ] Architecture data-flow diagram
   - [ ] LIA (if legitimate interests basis used)
   - [ ] AI Act high-risk system registration record

---

## 5. Ongoing Maintenance

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| Annual calendar review | Re-assess DPIA; update if processing unchanged; re-obtain DPO sign-off |
| Material change to data flows (new fields, new system) | Initiate DPIA change request in OneTrust immediately |
| New Azure OpenAI model version or feature | Review Microsoft DPA / model card; update risk section |
| Regulatory guidance update (EU AI Act implementing acts) | Update classification section; notify DPO |
| Security incident involving HR AI data | Trigger DPIA re-assessment; notify DPO within 24 hours |

> **TODO:** Schedule annual DPIA review in OneTrust as a recurring task assigned to `<Privacy Program Manager>`.

---

## 6. References

- GDPR Art. 35 — Data Protection Impact Assessment
- GDPR Art. 9 — Processing of special categories
