  --service-name <search-service-name> \
  --resource-group <resource-group>

# Compare output against Section 2 allowlist; flag any data source not listed above.
```

---

## 4. Change Control Process — Adding or Modifying a Source

### Step 1 — Change Request Submission
- Requester opens an HR Service Delivery ticket (category: `AI System / RAG Corpus Change`) including:
  - Proposed source (URL, endpoint, table, field list)
  - Business justification
  - Data classification of proposed content
  - Risk assessment (does it introduce sensitive categories currently out of scope?)
  - Proposed indexer field mapping changes

### Step 2 — HR Corpus Owner Review (SLA: 5 business days)
- Named HR Corpus Owner (`TODO: name`) reviews the request against:
  - [ ] Data minimisation — only fields needed for RAG retrieval quality
  - [ ] Sensitive category check — no salary, health, biometric, disciplinary free-text without a separate DPIA/risk assessment
  - [ ] Purview Information Protection label — source must not be labelled `Confidential\HighlyRestricted` unless a separate control review is completed
  - [ ] Azure AI Search index schema impact
  - [ ] Legal / privacy sign-off (if new sensitive category)

### Step 3 — Approval or Rejection
- **Approved:** Corpus Owner adds the source to this document (new row, status `APPROVED`), increments the SharePoint major version, and records their name + date.
- **Rejected:** Corpus Owner closes the ticket with reason. No indexer change is made.

### Step 4 — Terraform / Indexer Update
- Engineer updates the Azure AI Search indexer Terraform (or ARM) configuration to reflect the newly approved scope.
- Pull request must reference the HR Service Delivery ticket number and the SharePoint version number of this document.
- PR reviewer confirms field mappings match the allowlist before merge.

### Step 5 — Post-Change Verification
- After deployment, engineer confirms via Azure Portal / CLI that the new indexer data source and field mappings exactly match the approved entry.
- Corpus Owner is notified of completion.

