INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('9f419cbd-a020-4b19-967b-c9ae10c64a86', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 2, 'Ensure all ~100 employees access the Meeting Note Cleanup Assistant through the organization-managed OpenAI API account — not personal ChatGPT accounts — with individual API keys or authenticated sessions traceable to each user.', 'The client confirmed ''no business'' (ChatGPT Business) and users may be on personal accounts, meaning no organizational control over data retention, training opt-out, or audit.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.2; A.6.2.4","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 1.1; MANAGE 2.2"}'::jsonb, 'In the OpenAI API platform (platform.openai.com), create an Organization for this use case. Add all ~100 authorized users as members. Issue per-user API keys or route through an internal thin wrapper app that authenticates users before proxying to the OpenAI API. Update the AUP to explicitly state: ''Do not use personal ChatGPT consumer accounts (chat.openai.com) for cleaning business meeting notes — all usage must go through the company OpenAI API account.''', 'OpenAI API organization membership list showing all authorized users, and confirmation that personal ChatGPT consumer accounts are prohibited for this workflow in the AUP.', 'Export the OpenAI API organization member list and compare against the ~100 authorized users; separately, confirm the AUP explicitly prohibits use of personal ChatGPT accounts for business meeting notes.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('c93623f5-c473-452c-8e89-8c536110f3f0', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 3, 'Publish an explicit data boundary rule in the AUP specifying which content categories are prohibited from being pasted into the Meeting Note Cleanup Assistant: notes from HR investigations, legal/M&A discussions, regulated personal data (GDPR subjects, health info), client financials, MNPI, security incidents, and credential/authentication details.', 'There is currently no technical or policy mechanism preventing employees from pasting regulated or highly sensitive meeting notes — the data boundary is entirely honor-system.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 10 (data governance); Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.7.4; A.8.2","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 1.1; MAP 5.1; MANAGE 2.2"}'::jsonb, 'Update the organization''s Acceptable Use Policy to add a section titled ''AI Tool Data Boundaries — Meeting Note Cleanup Assistant''. List prohibited categories: (1) HR/personnel investigation notes, (2) legal matter or M&A discussion notes, (3) personal data of EU/UK residents, (4) client financial data or deal terms, (5) security incident details, (6) credentials or access tokens. Distribute via the existing AUP acknowledgment process. Require re-acknowledgment from all ~100 users.', 'AUP document or addendum with a dated, versioned section listing prohibited content categories for this specific AI use case, acknowledged by the Marketing team owner.', 'Review the AUP, confirm prohibited categories are explicitly listed with examples, and verify that at least a sample of 10 users have acknowledged the updated policy.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('a0990789-787b-40cc-ac88-1d44a494d7bc', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 3, 'Classify meeting notes submitted to this tool as ''Internal — may contain Confidential'' and enforce the data classification in the AUP such that notes classified Confidential or above are prohibited from submission.', 'Meeting notes inherently contain enterprise-relevant information (attendee names, project details, decisions) but there is no data classification applied before submission to the vendor AI.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 10 (data governance)","iso_42001":"A.7.4; A.8.2","owasp_llm":"LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 1.1; MAP 5.1"}'::jsonb, 'In the AUP data boundary section, add: ''Before pasting notes, assess their sensitivity. Notes containing only your own informal observations, task lists, and non-sensitive project references may be submitted. Notes containing client-identifiable information, financial figures, personnel discussions, or any Confidential-classified content must NOT be submitted.'' Provide 2-3 concrete before/after examples showing what an acceptable vs. prohibited note looks like.', 'Data classification policy mapping meeting notes to a classification level, and AUP language referencing the classification threshold above which submission to external AI is prohibited.', 'Review the data classification policy and AUP to confirm the classification threshold is stated and employees are instructed to self-classify notes before pasting; interview 5 users to confirm awareness.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('09bee149-1ddc-467f-99f1-7dfa7ec766f7', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 3, 'Deploy Microsoft Purview DLP to inspect and optionally block browser-based submissions to OpenAI endpoints containing sensitive data patterns (PII, client names from a managed list, financial terms).', 'The honor-system data boundary does not scale to 100 users — technical enforcement is needed to catch inadvertent sensitive data submissions.', 'recommended', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 10 (data governance); Art. 9 (risk management)","iso_42001":"A.7.4; A.8.4","owasp_llm":"LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 2.2; GOVERN 1.7"}'::jsonb, 'In the Microsoft Purview compliance portal, create a DLP policy scoped to the browser/endpoint channel. Add sensitive information types: (1) built-in PII types (SSN, passport, IBAN), (2) a custom sensitive info type using a keyword dictionary of top client names. Set the policy to apply to URLs matching ''api.openai.com'' and ''chat.openai.com''. Set action to ''Warn user and log'' initially, escalating to ''Block'' after a pilot period. Assign the policy to the ~100 Marketing team users. Note: Purview endpoint DLP requires Microsoft 365 E5 or E5 Compliance add-on and Purview endpoint agent on user devices.', 'Microsoft Purview DLP policy export showing rules targeting OpenAI API endpoints and/or chat.openai.com, with sensitive info types configured (e.g., PII, custom keyword dictionaries for client names) and action set to warn or block.', 'Submit a test note containing synthetic PII (e.g., a fake SSN or GDPR-subject name) through the same channel employees use and verify Purview flags or blocks the submission.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('479c667f-3f2c-47ad-a413-1249b25d33ab', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 3, 'Review and configure the OpenAI API organization settings to confirm that data submitted via the API is not used for model training, and document the data retention period.', 'The top risk is sensitive business information leaking to OpenAI — confirming training opt-out and understanding retention are the first technical mitigations.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 10 (data governance); Art. 12 (record-keeping)","iso_42001":"A.8.2; A.6.2.6","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 6.1; MAP 5.1; MANAGE 3.1"}'::jsonb, 'Log into platform.openai.com with the organization admin account. Navigate to Settings > Organization. Confirm the data usage policy states that API data is not used for training (this is the default for API usage as of 2024, but verify). Document the retention period (currently 30 days for abuse/safety monitoring). Save a screenshot with date. If the organization has a signed DPA with OpenAI (Enterprise tier), file a copy with the inventory record. If no DPA exists, flag to Legal/Privacy as a gap to close.', 'Screenshot or export of OpenAI API organization settings showing training opt-out status, plus documented data retention terms from the OpenAI API data usage policy or DPA.', 'Log into platform.openai.com, navigate to Organization > Settings, and verify that data is not used for training; cross-reference with the current OpenAI API data usage policy to confirm the retention window (currently 30 days for abuse monitoring).', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('9584a564-9598-451a-97f5-14bfbb33f586', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 5, 'Instruct employees in the AUP that AI-cleaned meeting notes must be reviewed before being saved into shared systems (wikis, Confluence, SharePoint, project tools) and that the employee — not the AI — is the author of record.', 'Employees confirmed they sometimes save AI outputs into shared systems; unchecked AI-formatted notes may contain hallucinated action items or inaccurate summaries that become treated as official records.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 14 (human oversight); Art. 13 (transparency)","iso_42001":"A.8.4; A.9.3","owasp_llm":"LLM09 Overreliance","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 2.2; MANAGE 3.1"}'::jsonb, 'Add to the AUP: ''Before saving AI-cleaned notes to any shared system (Confluence, SharePoint, Teams, Asana, etc.), you must: (1) Review the output for accuracy — confirm all action items, names, and decisions match your original notes, (2) Remove any AI-generated content that was not in your original notes, (3) Add a note at the bottom: "Formatting assisted by AI tool — reviewed by [your name]."'' Communicate this via the same channel used to distribute the AUP update.', 'AUP section stating that AI-generated output must be reviewed before sharing, the employee remains the author of record, and AI-cleaned notes saved to shared systems should be marked as ''AI-assisted formatting.''', 'Interview 5 users who save outputs to shared systems and confirm they review before saving; spot-check 3 shared documents for the AI-assisted attribution.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('0e2e0e9c-beed-4151-ba67-49d01d789338', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 7, 'Document the Marketing team lead as the accountable owner for this use case with explicit responsibilities: enforcing AUP compliance among users, responding to data incidents, conducting quarterly usage reviews, and deciding on scope changes.', 'Without a named accountable individual, the honor-system data boundary has no enforcement mechanism and incidents have no clear escalation owner.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.5.3; A.5.4","owasp_llm":"n/a","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 2.1; GOVERN 2.2"}'::jsonb, 'Create a one-page accountability document or RACI entry: Owner = [Marketing Team Lead name], Responsibilities = (1) Enforce AUP data boundaries for meeting note cleanup, (2) First responder for data incidents involving this tool, (3) Quarterly review of usage scope and user count, (4) Approve/deny scope expansion requests (e.g., adding new teams). Have the named owner sign and file with the AI inventory record.', 'Signed accountability statement or RACI entry naming the Marketing team lead, their specific responsibilities for this AI use case, and their escalation authority.', 'Confirm the named owner can describe the data boundary rules, the incident escalation path, and has conducted at least one usage review.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('a75a98c8-6c7b-4e57-8964-9a6d729e2ad3', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 7, 'Deliver lightweight user guidance (not just the AUP) to all ~100 users covering: what notes are safe to paste, what to never paste, how to review output, and how to report an accidental sensitive data submission.', 'The AUP sets policy but users need practical, memorable guidance to operationalize the data boundary — especially since the failure mode is someone not thinking twice before pasting sensitive notes.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 26 (deployer obligations); Art. 13 (transparency)","iso_42001":"A.4.3; A.4.6","owasp_llm":"LLM09 Overreliance","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 4.1; GOVERN 4.2"}'::jsonb, 'Create a one-page guide covering: (1) Safe to paste: your personal task lists, informal observations, non-sensitive project references, (2) Never paste: client names/financials, HR/legal discussion notes, PII, credentials, M&A content, (3) Before saving to shared systems: review for accuracy, add AI-assisted attribution, (4) If you accidentally paste something sensitive: immediately report to [incident email/channel] — do not wait. Distribute via email and pin in the team''s primary communication channel (Slack/Teams). Track acknowledgment.', 'One-page user guide or short training module distributed to all ~100 users, with delivery confirmation (email read receipts, LMS completion, or acknowledgment log).', 'Verify delivery records show >90% of the ~100 users received the guidance; quiz 5 random users on the key rules (what not to paste, how to report an incident).', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('551403da-41d5-4974-afcb-96a582eddf17', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 8, 'Before broader rollout or annual renewal, conduct a lightweight assurance test: submit 5 sample notes (including one with synthetic sensitive data) through the actual workflow and verify (a) the output is formatting-only with no hallucinated content, and (b) the Purview DLP policy (once deployed) catches the sensitive note.', 'The use case is live with ~100 users but there is no evidence it was tested before deployment — assurance testing validates that both the AI behavior and the controls work as expected.', 'recommended', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9 (risk management); Art. 15 (accuracy and robustness)","iso_42001":"A.9.4; A.9.5","owasp_llm":"LLM09 Overreliance","nist_ai_rmf":"MEASURE 2.6; MEASURE 2.7"}'::jsonb, 'Create 5 test notes: (1) clean project update notes, (2) notes with a few typos and disorganized bullets, (3) notes referencing a real-sounding but synthetic client name and deal value, (4) notes mentioning a fictional HR matter, (5) notes with a synthetic email address and phone number. Submit each through the OpenAI API using the standard system prompt. Document: did the output add content not in the input? Did it preserve sensitive terms? Did Purview (once deployed) flag notes 3-5? File the test report with the inventory record.', 'Test report documenting the 5 test notes, their outputs, pass/fail against formatting-only criteria, and DLP detection results, signed by the technical owner.', 'Review the test report for completeness; re-run one test case independently to verify reproducibility.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('b037a2e6-a773-40b4-a473-e2937853637f', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 9, 'Enable and retain OpenAI API usage logs capturing: timestamp, user identifier, model used, token count, and request metadata — but NOT full prompt content — to establish an audit trail of usage volume and patterns without creating a secondary sensitive data store.', 'There is currently no audit trail of what is being submitted to OpenAI, making it impossible to detect anomalous usage patterns or investigate incidents.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 12 (record-keeping); Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.6; A.9.6","owasp_llm":"LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure","nist_ai_rmf":"MEASURE 2.5; MANAGE 1.3"}'::jsonb, 'In the OpenAI API platform (platform.openai.com), navigate to Usage and confirm per-API-key usage tracking is active. If using a thin internal wrapper, add structured logging at the proxy layer capturing: timestamp, authenticated user ID, model name, prompt token count, completion token count — do NOT log prompt content (to avoid creating a secondary sensitive data store). Export logs to whatever centralized logging the org uses. If no centralized logging exists, retain the OpenAI platform usage dashboard exports monthly. Set retention to 90 days minimum.', 'OpenAI API usage dashboard or exported usage logs showing per-user request counts, token volumes, and timestamps for the last 30 days.', 'Export API usage data for the last 7 days and confirm it shows individual user attribution, request counts, and token volumes; verify retention is at least 90 days.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('c2e0af81-1093-42d4-a2ba-a8d7af1082ff', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 10, 'Document and communicate an incident response path specific to this use case: if an employee accidentally pastes sensitive data into the tool, they report to [defined channel], the business owner assesses severity, and the technical owner contacts OpenAI to request data deletion if warranted.', 'The client confirmed an incident process exists but the failure mode is someone pasting sensitive content without realizing it — the response path must be specific, known, and include the OpenAI data deletion request step.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 26 (deployer obligations); Art. 9 (risk management)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.8; A.9.7","owasp_llm":"LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 4.1; MANAGE 4.2"}'::jsonb, 'Document a one-page incident runbook: (1) Employee reports to [incident email or Slack channel] immediately, (2) Marketing team lead (business owner) triages: was the content truly sensitive? (3) If yes, technical owner submits a data deletion request to OpenAI via demo@community.example or the API support channel referencing the organization ID and approximate timestamp, (4) Business owner determines if further notification is needed (e.g., to the affected client or Legal), (5) Log the incident in the organization''s incident tracker. Distribute this runbook alongside the user guide.', 'Documented incident response procedure for this AI use case specifying: reporting channel, triage owner, severity criteria, OpenAI data deletion request process, and notification requirements.', 'Walk through a tabletop scenario with the business owner: ''An employee just pasted M&A discussion notes into the tool and realized 10 minutes later'' — verify they can describe each step of the response path including how to contact OpenAI for deletion.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('3adb093e-9379-44f3-911e-3d6e22d414fd', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '5576a726-ad6e-4da7-b9d9-6ca3ff8a030e', 10, 'Ensure the organization can disable all employee access to the OpenAI API for this use case within 1 business day by revoking API keys or disabling the organization, and document this as the kill switch procedure.', 'If a pattern of sensitive data leakage is discovered or OpenAI changes their data terms, the organization needs the ability to centrally halt all usage quickly.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T13:53:22.330005+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9 (risk management)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.8; A.9.8","owasp_llm":"LLM06 Excessive Agency","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 4.1; MANAGE 4.3"}'::jsonb, 'Document in the incident runbook: ''To disable all Meeting Note Cleanup Assistant usage: (1) Log into platform.openai.com with the organization admin account, (2) Navigate to API Keys, (3) Revoke all active API keys, or (4) If using an internal proxy, disable the proxy endpoint. Admin access holders: [Technical Owner name] (primary), [backup name] (secondary).'' Test that the technical owner has current admin credentials by having them log in (without revoking anything).', 'Documented kill switch procedure naming who has admin access to the OpenAI API organization and the steps to revoke all API keys or disable the organization.', 'Verify the technical owner can demonstrate (without executing) the steps to revoke all API keys in the OpenAI platform and confirm it would take less than 1 business day.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('4498977e-32af-4cb2-85a7-fe24afbf8bd7', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '84c9d8a0-f0da-43ca-8e3a-41c529bfbe9d', 1, 'Assign a named individual (not a team) as the accountable system owner for the Internal Helpdesk Assistant, with documented responsibility for accuracy, data boundary integrity, and incident escalation.', 'The current owner is ''Engineer team'' — a team cannot be held accountable; a named individual must own risk decisions, approve corpus changes, and respond to incidents.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-09T03:25:55.430552+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9(2) (risk management responsibility); Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.4.3; A.5.2","owasp_llm":"n/a","nist_ai_rmf":"GOVERN 1.2; GOVERN 2.1"}'::jsonb, 'In Drata, update the AI asset record to assign a single named individual as the control owner. In Jira, create a project for ''Helpdesk Assistant Governance'' and set that individual as project lead. Document their responsibilities in a linked Confluence page: corpus approval authority, incident escalation decision-maker, accuracy complaint triage owner.', 'Drata control owner assignment or Jira project lead designation showing a single named individual with documented responsibilities.', 'Verify a named individual (not a team or distribution list) is recorded as system owner in Drata and can describe their responsibilities when asked.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'runbook', 'markdown', '4498977e-helpdesk-assistant-ownership-assignment.md', '# Control 4498977e: AI System Ownership & Accountability

**Purpose:** Assign a named individual (not a team) as the accountable system owner for the Internal Helpdesk Assistant, with documented responsibility for accuracy, data boundary integrity, and incident escalation.

**Audience:** Security, GRC, Helpdesk leadership  
**Status:** Review before implementation

---

## Task 1: Identify and Designate System Owner

1. **Stakeholders:** Meet with Helpdesk leadership, Security, and Data teams.
2. **Selection Criteria:**
   - Deep knowledge of Helpdesk Assistant corpus, use cases, and data boundaries
   - Authority to approve corpus updates and policy changes
   - Ability to respond to incidents within defined SLAs (e.g., within 4 hours for escalation)
   - Willingness to accept named accountability
3. **Assignment:**
   - **Designated Owner (to be filled in):** `[TODO: Full name, title, contact email]`
   - **Start Date:** `[TODO: Date assignment becomes effective]`
   - **Backup Owner (optional but recommended):** `[TODO: Full name, title, contact email]`

---

## Task 2: Update Drata AI Asset Record

1. **Login to Drata** as a GRC admin or control owner.
2. **Navigate** to the AI Assets or Inventory section.
3. **Search for or create** the "Internal Helpdesk Assistant" asset record.
4. **Update the following fields:**
   - **Control Owner:** Change from "Engineer team" to the designated individual''s name (from Task 1).
   - **Owner Email:** Add their email address for notifications.
   - **Owner Phone/On-call Info:** Add escalation contact details (optional).
   - **Effective Date:** Set the assignment date.
   - **Notes:** "Assigned as named accountable owner per control 4498977e. Responsibilities: corpus approval, incident escalation, accuracy oversight."
5. **Save** and confirm the change is logged in Drata''s audit trail.
6. **Verification:** Drata should display the owner name on all future control assessments and reports.

---

## Task 3: Create Jira Project for Helpdesk Assistant Governance

1. **Login to Jira** as a project admin.
2. **Create a new project:**
   - **Project Key:** `HAG` (e.g., "Helpdesk Assistant Governance")
   - **Project Name:** "Helpdesk Assistant Governance"
   - **Project Type:** Choose "Business" (or equivalent for governance/process work)
3. **Assign Project Lead:**
   - Set the designated owner (from Task 1) as the **Project Lead**.
   - Assign initial team members: Security champion, Data steward, Helpdesk manager.
4. **Create initial issue templates/epics:**
   - Epic: "Corpus Management" (for change requests, updates, retraining)
   - Epic: "Incident Response" (for accuracy complaints, data boundary breaches)
   - Epic: "Audit & Compliance" (for regular reviews, Drata updates)
5. **Configure project permissions:** Ensure the Project Lead can create, update, and resolve issues.
6. **Document in Jira Description:** Link to Confluence page (created in Task 4).

---

## Task 4: Document Responsibilities in Confluence

1. **Create a Confluence page** titled: "Internal Helpdesk Assistant — System Owner Responsibilities"
   - **Parent Page:** Link to your organization''s AI governance or Helpdesk governance space.
   - **Accessibility:** Set permissions so all Helpdesk and Security teams can read; owner can edit.

2. **Document the following sections:**

   ### Authority & Scope
   - Owner has final authority to approve or reject corpus updates, retraining decisions, and policy changes.
   - Owner must review and sign off on any changes to system prompts, knowledge base, or data sources.

   ### Incident Escalation
   - Owner is the primary decision-maker for:
     - Accuracy complaints (false/misleading responses)
     - Data boundary violations (system accessing unauthorized data)
     - Security incidents (prompt injection, unauthorized tool use)
   - **Escalation SLA:** Owner must acknowledge critical incidents within `[TODO: e.g., 4 hours]` and propose remediation within `[TODO: e.g., 24 hours]`.
   - Owner escalates to CISO or Legal as needed.

   ### Accuracy & Quality Oversight
   - Owner owns accuracy metrics and targets (e.g., "95% accuracy on Tier-1 queries").
   - Owner must review monthly accuracy reports and approve remedial retraining.
   - Owner is the triage owner for user-reported accuracy complaints (logs them in Jira, assigns investigation).

   ### Data Boundary Integrity
   - Owner reviews and approves all data sources connected to the Helpdesk Assistant.
   - Owner must validate that the system does not access or expose sensitive data outside its intended scope (e.g., employee PII, financial records).
   - Owner coordinates with Data/Security to audit data access logs quarterly.

   ### Governance & Compliance
   - Owner updates Drata records when corpus, ownership, or scope changes.
   - Owner participates in quarterly AI governance reviews.
   - Owner maintains a change log of all approved updates (linked Jira project).

   ### Contact & On-Call
   - **Owner Name & Title:** `[TODO: Insert from Task 1]`
   - **Email:** `[TODO: Insert from Task 1]`
   - **On-Call/Escalation:** `[TODO: Insert backup or on-call schedule]`
   - **Office Hours / Response SLA:** `[TODO: e.g., "Business hours, 4-hour acknowledgment SLA for critical incidents"]`

3. **Link this page in:**
   - Drata AI asset record (field: "Documentation URL")
   - Jira project description
   - Internal wiki/onboarding docs for Helpdesk Assistant

---

## Task 5: Notify & Train the Owner

1. **Send formal notification** to the designated owner outlining their new accountability.
2. **Schedule a kickoff meeting** with:
   - Owner
   - Security lead
   - Helpdesk manager
   - Data steward
   - GRC/Drata admin
3. **Walk through:**
   - Confluence responsibility document
   - Jira project workflow
   - Drata update process
   - Incident escalation path
   - Quarterly review cadence
4. **Confirm owner''s understanding** and sign-off (optional: email confirmation or light MOU).

---

## Completion Checklist

- [ ] Named individual identified and agreed to accountability
- [ ] Drata AI asset record updated with owner name and email
- [ ] Jira "Helpdesk Assistant Governance" project created with owner as Project Lead
- [ ] Confluence responsibility page created and linked in Drata & Jira
- [ ] Owner trained on responsibilities and escalation procedures
- [ ] Backup owner designated (if applicable)
- [ ] Email notification sent to stakeholders confirming ownership change
- [ ] Initial audit log entry created in Drata documenting the assignment

---

