# GitHub Copilot Acceptable Use Policy

**Version:** 1.0 <!-- TODO: increment on each review -->
**Owner:** <!-- TODO: Engineering VP name --> (Business) / <!-- TODO: Platform Lead name --> (Technical)
**Effective Date:** <!-- TODO: YYYY-MM-DD -->
**Review Cadence:** Quarterly (see Jira recurring task — <!-- TODO: insert Jira ticket ID -->)
**Evidence Location:** OneTrust AI Inventory → GitHub Copilot asset → Documents tab <!-- TODO: confirm asset name/ID -->

---

## 1. Purpose

This policy governs the use of GitHub Copilot across all engineering teams. Copilot accelerates development but introduces specific risks — including insecure code patterns, license-contaminated suggestions, and credential-adjacent outputs — that require deliberate human review at every step.

---

## 2. Scope

Applies to **all engineers holding a GitHub Copilot license** in the <!-- TODO: Org name --> GitHub organization. Covers all Copilot surfaces: IDE extensions (VS Code, JetBrains, etc.), Copilot Chat, and any future Copilot features enabled at the org level.

---

## 3. Mandatory Review Requirements

| Rule | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **R1 — Read before accepting** | Every suggestion MUST be read and understood before acceptance. Bulk/tab-accept of multi-line suggestions without review is prohibited. |
| **R2 — No auto-accept plugins** | IDE plugins or scripts that automatically accept suggestions without human review are **prohibited**. |
| **R3 — IaC extra scrutiny** | All Copilot-generated Terraform, Kubernetes manifests, and Cloud Function configs MUST pass `terraform plan` + the automated security scan (checkov/tfsec) before merge. |
| **R4 — No secrets in context** | Do not open files containing secrets, tokens, or credentials while Copilot is active. Copilot has context over all open files in your IDE session. |
| **R5 — PR review required** | All Copilot-assisted code must go through the standard peer review process (min 1 human approval). See branch protection policy. |

---

## 4. What Copilot Can See

- **All files open in your IDE** at the time of a suggestion request.
- **Your accessible repository context** — Copilot uses the current file, surrounding code, and open tabs as context. This includes any IaC files, config files, or environment-specific values that are open.
- **It does NOT see** other repos you have access to unless those files are open in your editor.

> ⚠️ **Do not open `.env` files, `terraform.tfvars` with real secrets, or any file containing credentials while Copilot is active.**

---

## 5. IaC-Specific Guidance

- Treat all Copilot-generated Terraform and Kubernetes output as **untrusted draft code**.
- Always run `terraform plan` and review the diff before merging.
- The CI pipeline will block merges that fail HIGH/CRITICAL checkov findings — do not attempt to suppress findings without documented justification and technical owner approval.
- Pay particular attention to: IAM bindings, KMS key policies, GKE node pool configs, Cloud Function service account assignments, and network/firewall rules.

---

## 6. How to Report Concerning Suggestions

If Copilot produces a suggestion that appears to:
- Contain a hardcoded secret or credential pattern
- Suggest an excessively permissive IAM or network rule
- Reproduce what appears to be verbatim third-party licensed code
- Exhibit unexpected or anomalous behavior

**Action:** Open a Jira ticket of type **`AI-Concern`** in the <!-- TODO: insert Jira project key --> project, including:
1. A description of the suggestion (do not paste actual secrets)
2. The repository and file type context
3. Your assessment of the risk

The Technical Owner (<!-- TODO: Platform Lead name -->) will triage within 2 business days.

---

## 7. Acknowledgment & Onboarding

- A Jira task of type `Copilot-AUP-Acknowledgment` will be assigned to each Copilot-licensed engineer upon license grant. <!-- TODO: confirm Jira automation is configured to create these tasks -->
- Engineers must complete the task (confirming they have read this policy) **within 5 business days** of license grant.
- Signed acknowledgments are stored in OneTrust as evidence. <!-- TODO: confirm OneTrust document upload workflow -->
- This policy is linked from the Copilot onboarding email template. <!-- TODO: update onboarding email template -->

---

## 8. Violations

Violations of this policy (e.g., merging auto-accepted IaC without review, suppressing security scans without approval) should be reported to the Technical Owner and may result in license suspension pending review.

---

