# Runbook: GitHub Copilot Data Processing Agreement (DPA) Review

## Purpose
Ensure the GitHub/Microsoft Copilot Data Processing Agreement is reviewed, uploaded to OneTrust Vendor Risk Management, and all data-handling commitments are documented and signed-off by Legal.

---

## Prerequisites
- OneTrust Vendor Risk Management module accessible
- Legal counsel with authority to review and sign off DPAs
- Access to Microsoft Licensing Portal (or Microsoft 365 Admin Center)
- GitHub Enterprise Cloud or Copilot for Business subscription active

---

## Step 1 — Obtain the Current DPA

1. Log into the **Microsoft Licensing Portal**: https://www.microsoft.com/licensing/docs
   > `# TODO: Confirm the correct portal URL for your Microsoft Enterprise Agreement — it may be VLSC or Microsoft 365 Admin Center > Billing > Agreements.`
2. Locate the **GitHub Copilot for Business Data Protection Agreement** (DPA).
   - Also available publicly at: https://github.com/customer-terms/github-data-protection-agreement
3. Download the current PDF version and note the **version date**.
4. Cross-reference with the **Microsoft Online Services DPA** if applicable to your EA:
   - https://aka.ms/DPA

---

## Step 2 — Create/Update OneTrust Vendor Record

1. Navigate to **OneTrust** → **Vendor Risk Management** → **Vendors**.
2. Search for `GitHub` or `Microsoft`. If no record exists, click **+ Add Vendor**.
3. Set the following fields:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Vendor Name | `GitHub, Inc. / Microsoft Corporation` |
| Service | `GitHub Copilot for Business / Enterprise` |
| Vendor Tier | `Tier 1 — Critical` |
| Data Categories Shared | Proprietary source code, IaC configs, internal libraries |
| Data Classification | Confidential / Proprietary |
| Assessment Status | `In Review` |

> `# TODO: Adjust vendor tier per your internal tiering criteria.`

---

## Step 3 — Document Key DPA Commitments

Record the following in the OneTrust vendor record under **Data Processing Details**:

### 3.1 Data Retention & Processing

| Commitment | GitHub/Microsoft Published Position | Verified? |
|---|---|---|
| Code processed in real-time | Yes — code is not stored post-response per GitHub''s DPA §X | `# TODO: Verify exact section reference in downloaded DPA` |
| Prompt/suggestion retention | Transient only (milliseconds) — not persisted | `# TODO: Confirm version date` |
| Training opt-out honored | Yes, when org-level opt-out is configured (see control 47300265) | `# TODO: Cross-reference settings screenshot` |
| Logs retention period | `# TODO: Document from DPA — typically 28 days for telemetry if not opted out` | |

### 3.2 Data Residency

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Processing region(s) | `# TODO: Confirm from DPA — typically US; EU customers may have different terms` |
| In-region processing available? | `# TODO: Check if your EA includes GitHub Enterprise with data residency options` |
| Org data residency requirement | `# TODO: Insert your org''s required data region` |
| Residency gap? | `# TODO: Yes / No — if Yes, raise with Legal and record risk acceptance` |

### 3.3 Sub-Processors

1. Download the current sub-processor list from:
   - https://github.com/github/site-policy/blob/main/Policies/github-subprocessors-and-cookies.md
   - Microsoft sub-processors: https://aka.ms/Online_Serv_Subprocessors_Audit
2. Upload to OneTrust attachment section.
3. Record the date retrieved and schedule a 6-month refresh.

> `# TODO: List key sub-processors identified (e.g., Azure OpenAI Service, Azure infrastructure) in the OneTrust record.`

### 3.4 Deletion Commitments

| Commitment | DPA Reference | Verified? |
|---|---|---|
| On contract termination, data deleted within X days | `# TODO: Insert days from DPA` | |
| Deletion certificate available on request | `# TODO: Yes / No` | |

---

## Step 4 — Legal Review & Sign-Off

1. Assign the OneTrust vendor record to **Legal Counsel** for DPA review.
2. Legal must confirm:
   - [ ] DPA version reviewed and date recorded
   - [ ] Data residency requirements met (or risk accepted)
   - [ ] Sub-processor list reviewed — no prohibited jurisdictions
   - [ ] Deletion commitments acceptable
   - [ ] Training opt-out clause confirmed in DPA language
3. Legal signs off in OneTrust using the **Approval Workflow**.
4. Record the sign-off date and reviewer name in the vendor record.

> `# TODO: Set the Legal Counsel''s OneTrust user account as the approval task owner.`

---

## Step 5 — Link to AI Asset Inventory Record

1. In OneTrust, open the **GitHub Copilot AI Asset Record** (created per control a288a7fa).
2. Link this Vendor Risk record to the AI Asset record via **Related Records**.
3. Confirm the DPA review date populates as a review condition for the 90-day recertification cycle.

---

## Step 6 — Schedule Annual DPA Re-Review

Create a Jira task for annual DPA re-review:

```
