## 3. Incident Classification

| Severity | Definition | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **P1 — Critical** | Personal data exfiltrated; discriminatory action taken on employee; active RBAC/injection exploit in progress | RBAC bypass exposing bulk employee records |
| **P2 — High** | Biased draft acted upon; missed escalation on high-risk case; confirmed injection payload in case note | Termination letter generated without required legal review |
| **P3 — Medium** | Unauthorized retrieval contained to single session; suspicious query pattern detected | Single user queried records outside their HRBP scope |
| **P4 — Low** | Anomalous but non-harmful behaviour; near-miss; policy clarification required | Unusual prompt structure, no data returned |

