INSERT INTO control_items ("id", "org_id", "use_case_id", "pillar", "control", "why", "requirement", "status", "owner", "created_at", "framework_refs", "stack_implementation", "evidence", "assurance_test", "verification_status", "verification_mode", "verification_note", "verified_by", "verified_at", "artifact_type", "artifact_language", "artifact_filename", "artifact_content", "artifact_generated_at", "capability_id", "evidence_url") VALUES ('58143798-6de7-4159-8f92-f0457e374411', '00000000-0000-4000-a000-0000000000de', '159c61b4-30e3-40d4-88f0-f5a4b1d66b1b', 10, 'Define incident escalation path and restart criteria: the engineering team must have a documented escalation path (who to notify, in what order, via what channel) for agent incidents, and the agent may not be restarted after a kill-switch activation without explicit sign-off from the residual risk owner.', 'The agent is in production handling real customer data; without a defined escalation path and restart criteria, incident response is ad-hoc and premature restart risks repeating the same failure.', 'required', 'gap', NULL, '2026-06-08T11:06:43.005587+00:00', '{"eu_ai_act":"Art. 9 (risk management); Art. 26 (deployer obligations)","iso_42001":"A.6.2.8; A.9.4","owasp_llm":"LLM10 Unbounded Consumption","nist_ai_rmf":"MANAGE 4.1; MANAGE 4.2; GOVERN 6.2"}'::jsonb, 'Create a runbook at /runbooks/incident-escalation.md: Step 1 — Engineering team activates kill switch and posts in #onboarding-agent-incidents Slack channel. Step 2 — Page the on-call engineer via PagerDuty (configure a PagerDuty service ''Onboarding Agent'' with the engineering team rotation). Step 3 — Notify the residual risk owner and security team. Step 4 — Begin investigation using Google Chronicle logs. Restart criteria: risk owner must comment ''Approved to restart'' on the incident Jira ticket with a root-cause summary before the GKE deployment is scaled back up. Add a GitHub Actions workflow that requires manual approval from the risk owner''s GitHub account before running the restart script.', 'Incident response runbook documenting escalation path (names, channels, SLAs) and restart criteria (sign-off requirement); PagerDuty or equivalent configuration for the engineering team.', 'Simulate a kill-switch activation; confirm the escalation notifications fire to the correct individuals in the correct order; attempt to restart the agent without risk-owner sign-off and confirm it is blocked or flagged.', 'not_checked', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'runbook', 'markdown', 'incident-escalation.md', '# Agent Incident Escalation & Restart Runbook

Control ref: `58143798-6de7-4159-8f92-f0457e374411` (Pillar 10)

This runbook defines the escalation path for LangChain agent incidents in production and the explicit sign-off criteria required before restart.

---

## Incident Escalation Path

### Step 1: Kill-Switch Activation & Notification

**When:** An engineer detects an agent failure, data exfiltration risk, or runaway autonomy that requires immediate shutdown.

**Action:**
1. Activate the kill switch immediately (deployment scale-down or pod termination).
2. Post incident alert in **#onboarding-agent-incidents** Slack channel with:
   - Timestamp and affected GKE cluster/namespace
   - Brief description of the incident (e.g., "Agent making unauthorized API calls to Salesforce")
   - Initial severity (Critical/High/Medium)
   - Your name and on-call rotation member ID

**Example message:**
```
⚠️ AGENT INCIDENT - KILL SWITCH ACTIVATED
Cluster: us-central1-gke-prod
Namespace: onboarding-agent
Issue: Agent exceeded autonomy threshold; unauthorized Salesforce queries detected
Severity: Critical
Officer: @oncall-eng-tue
```

### Step 2: Page On-Call Engineer via PagerDuty

**Action:**
1. Trigger a PagerDuty incident for the **"Onboarding Agent"** service (must be configured in PagerDuty with the engineering team on-call rotation).
2. Include in the incident description:
   - Link to #onboarding-agent-incidents Slack thread
   - Severity level
   - Initial hypothesis (if any)

**PagerDuty Service Setup (Configuration Only):**
- **Service Name:** Onboarding Agent
- **Escalation Policy:** Engineering team primary on-call → Secondary on-call (if no ack within 5 min) → Engineering Manager (if no ack within 10 min)
- **Notification Channels:** Email + SMS for critical incidents
- **TODO:** Confirm PagerDuty service "Onboarding Agent" is created and the engineering team rotation is configured in PagerDuty console.

### Step 3: Notify Residual Risk Owner & Security Team

**Action:**
1. Notify the **Residual Risk Owner** (TODO: insert name/email, typically Security Lead or Compliance Officer).
2. Notify the **Security Team Lead** (TODO: insert name/email).
3. Use direct message + @mention in Slack to ensure immediate visibility.
4. Include:
   - PagerDuty incident URL
   - Slack thread link
   - Initial severity assessment

**Example notification:**
```
Subject: 🚨 Agent Incident - Escalation Required
To: TODO_RISK_OWNER_EMAIL, TODO_SECURITY_LEAD_EMAIL

Agent incident escalated in production. Kill switch activated.
PagerDuty: [link]
Slack: [link to thread]
Details: See Slack thread
```

### Step 4: Begin Investigation Using Google Chronicle

**Action:**
1. Access **Google Chronicle** console at `https://chronicle.YOUR_DOMAIN.com` (TODO: insert your Chronicle instance URL).
2. Query the agent pod logs and API call timeline:
   - **Log source:** GKE pod logs (namespace: `onboarding-agent`, pod prefix: `agent-*`)
   - **Key fields to investigate:**
     - Pod name, timestamp, error/exit code
     - Outbound API calls (destination, method, data exfiltrated)
     - LangChain tool invocations (which tools, arguments, responses)
     - Authentication failures or privilege escalation attempts
3. Document findings in a **Jira ticket** (see next section).
4. Share key findings in the Slack thread to keep team aligned.

**Example Chronicle query (pseudo-YARA/UDM):**
```
resource.type = "k8s_pod"
namespace = "onboarding-agent"
pod_name =~ "agent-.*"
| filter severity >= "ERROR"
| group_by metadata.event_timestamp, resource.pod_name, payload.message
| order by metadata.event_timestamp desc
```

---

## Restart Criteria & Approval Workflow

### Create Jira Incident Ticket

**Immediately after escalation:**
1. Create a **Jira issue** in the `ONBOARDING-AGENT` project (TODO: confirm project key).
2. **Issue type:** Incident
3. **Title:** `[INCIDENT] Agent Kill-Switch Activated - <date> <time>`
4. **Description:**
   ```
   **Incident Summary**
   - Time activated: [UTC timestamp]
   - Affected cluster/namespace: [GKE resource]
   - Initial hypothesis: [description from Slack]
   - Severity: [Critical/High/Medium]
   
   **Investigation**
   - Google Chronicle findings: [link or summary]
   - Root cause: [TODO - to be filled during investigation]
   
   **Restart Authorization**
   - Approved by: [TODO - Risk Owner]
   - Approval comment: [TODO - ''Approved to restart'' + root-cause summary]
   - Date/time approved: [TODO]
   ```
5. **Assign to:** On-call engineer (from PagerDuty)
6. **Add labels:** `incident`, `agent`, `kill-switch`
7. **Link blocking issue:** If applicable (e.g., Bug ticket for the root cause)

### Restart Authorization Gate

**Mandatory sign-off before restart:**

1. **Residual Risk Owner Review:**
   - The Residual Risk Owner (TODO: insert GitHub username) **must** review the incident summary and root-cause analysis in the Jira ticket.
   - They must explicitly comment on the Jira ticket:
     ```
     Approved to restart. Root cause: [summary of root cause]. Mitigation: [steps to prevent recurrence].
     ```
   - **This comment is mandatory; the ticket cannot proceed to restart without it.**

2. **GitHub Actions Workflow Approval:**
   - A GitHub Actions workflow (file: `.github/workflows/agent-restart.yml`) is triggered to scale the GKE deployment back to its original replicas.
   - **Approval requirement:** The workflow requires a manual approval from the Residual Risk Owner''s GitHub account (or a designated approver with role `risk-owner`).
   - Workflow will not execute the restart script until approval is granted.
   - Only then does the GKE deployment scale up.

**GitHub Actions Workflow (Scaffold):**
```yaml
name: Agent Restart - Risk Owner Approval Required

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      jira_ticket_id:
        description: "JIRA ticket ID (e.g., ONBOARDING-AGENT-123)"
        required: true
      cluster_name:
        description: "GKE cluster name"
        required: true

jobs:
  request-approval:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Validate JIRA Ticket
        run: |
          # TODO: Use Jira API to confirm ticket has ''Approved to restart'' comment from risk owner
          echo "Checking JIRA ticket ${{ github.event.inputs.jira_ticket_id }} for approval comment..."
          # curl -X GET https://TODO_JIRA_DOMAIN/rest/api/3/issues/$TICKET_ID/comments \
          #   -H "Authorization: Bearer ${{ secrets.JIRA_API_TOKEN }}"
          # Parse response for ''Approved to restart'' comment from TODO_RISK_OWNER_GITHUB_USER

      - name: Manual Approval Gate
        uses: trstringer/manual-approval@v1
        with:
          secret: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          approvers: TODO_RISK_OWNER_GITHUB_USER
          issue-title: "Approve restart for ${{ github.event.inputs.jira_ticket_id }}"
          issue-body: |
            Restart request for GKE agent deployment.
            Ticket: ${{ github.event.inputs.jira_ticket_id }}
            Cluster: ${{ github.event.inputs.cluster_name }}
            Please confirm in JIRA ticket that root cause is understood and mitigations are in place.

      - name: Scale Up GKE Deployment
        run: |
          # TODO: Configure gcloud CLI with credentials for GCP project
          gcloud container clusters get-credentials ${{ github.event.inputs.cluster_name }} --zone us-central1-a
          kubectl set replicas deployment/onboarding-agent --replicas=3 -n onboarding-agent
          kubectl rollout status deployment/onboarding-agent -n onboarding-agent --timeout=5m
          echo "✅ Agent deployment restarted and healthy."

      - name: Notify Slack - Restart Complete
        run: |
          # TODO: Configure Slack webhook URL in GitHub Secrets
          curl -X POST ${{ secrets.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL }} \
            -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' \
            -d ''{
              "text": "✅ Agent restart approved and completed",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "section",
                  "text": {
                    "type": "mrkdwn",
                    "text": "*Agent Restart Completed*\nJIRA: ${{ github.event.inputs.jira_ticket_id }}\nCluster: ${{ github.event.inputs.cluster_name }}\nApproved by: @${{ env.APPROVER }}"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }''
```

